    "https://www.ohio.edu/hr/jobs/student-employment": {
      "title": "Student Employment",
      "description": "Student Employment | Ohio University Skip to main content Close Search Search within: Human Resources ohio.edu Info for... Info for: Future Students Parents/Families Alumni/Friends Current Students Faculty/Staff Quick Links Log In Catmail Canvas MyOHIO Student Center Library Account Locations Visit Athens Campus Regional Campuses OHIO Online Connect Faculty/Staff Directory Contact Us Apply Give Search Search Menu Human Resources Employee Resources HR Quicklinks My Personal Information Workforce Forms Policies and Notices Employee Perks and Discounts Calendars Employment & Life Changes Hire & Manage Performance Management Hiring & Search Resources Onboarding Tools Employee Lookup Hiring Student Employees Employee Recognition Guide Access PeopleAdmin Labor Relations Labor (Union) Relations Faculty Petition for Representation Collective Bargaining Agreements Seniority Roster Workplace Support Employee Resources for Accessibility HR Business Partners by Planning Unit OHIO FlexWork Benefits Health & Insurance Benefits Benefits Guides Eligibility Premiums Disability Changing & Managing Benefits Retirement & Financial Planning Financial Wellness Preparing to Retire Retirement Plan Options Retirement@Work Supplemental Accounts Educational & Wellness Educational Benefits Worklife and Wellbeing Leave & Time Off Holiday Schedule Sick & Personal Time Vacation Time Leaves Winter Break Closure Compensation & Pay Pay Structures Payroll Schedules Payroll Services Salary Database Total Compensation Estimator OHIO Jobs Job Postings Student Employment Opportunities for Spouses / Partners Professional Development at OHIO Campus and Community Culture Working at OHIO Center For Employee Excellence Professional Development Professional Development Catalog Learning Experiences Helpful Links Info for... Info for: Future Students Parents/Families Alumni/Friends Current Students Faculty/Staff Quick Links Log In Catmail Canvas MyOHIO Student Center Library Account Locations Visit Athens Campus Regional Campuses OHIO Online Connect Faculty/Staff Directory Contact Us Apply Give Search Navigate OHIO About OHIO Admission Athletics Academics Life at OHIO Connect With Us Human Resources Grosvenor West 103 1 Ohio University Athens, OH 45701 Directions uhr@ohio.edu 740.593.1636 Human Resources Breadcrumb OHIO University Human Resources Ohio University Jobs Student Employment Student Employment Site-specific navigation Job Postings Student Employment Retirement Exemption Student Employment Eligibility Student Professional Etiquette Opportunities for Spouses / Partners Professional Development at OHIO Eligibility for Student Hourly Employment In order to be eligible for student employment at Ohio University, student must meet the following requirements: Comply with the Immigration Control and Reform Act of 1986 by completing a valid I-9 form within 72 hours of the start date of employment. Be enrolled for classes at Ohio University, Hocking College, another post-secondary education institution, or a secondary school during the current semester, immediate previous semester, or immediate upcoming semester. Non-Ohio University students must provide verification of student status to the hiring department. Additional eligibility restrictions apply for Federal Work Study and PACE positions. Refer to section on Types of Student Employment for additional information. Graduating students are eligible to continue working with the following limitations: Graduating Semester Continuation of work limited to: Fall Semester End of Winter Break Spring Semester End of 1 st Summer Session 1 st Summer Session End of 2 nd Summer Session 2 nd Summer Session or Full Summer Session September 30 Student Work Hour Limit Undergraduate students Undergrad student employees without an F or J Visa are permitted to work for the university as follows: Fall and spring semester: up to 25 hours per week Summer semester and all academic breaks: up to 36 hours per week Undergrad student employees with an F or J Visa are permitted to work for the university as follows: Fall and spring semester: up to 20 hours per week Summer semester and all academic breaks: up to 36 hours per week Graduate students Graduate students without an F or J Visa: With a graduate appointment that includes a stipend (GA, TA, RA, GRS, and RD), are permitted to work as follows: Fall semester: up to 20 hours per week Spring semester: up to 20 hours per week Summer semester: up to 20 hours per week With a graduate appointment that does NOT include a stipend, are permitted to work as follows: Fall and spring semester: up to 25 hours per week Summer semester and all academic breaks: up to 36 hours per week Graduate students with an F or J Visa: With a graduate appointment that includes a stipend, are permitted to work as follows: Fall semester: up to 20 hours per week Spring semester: up to 20 hours per week Summer semester: up to 20 hours per week With a graduate appointment that does NOT include a stipend, are permitted to work as follows: Fall and spring semester: up to 20 hours per week Summer semester and all academic breaks: up to 36 hours per week Types of Student Employment Student Hourly Employment Students who are not eligible for Federal Work Study or PACE, and are still interested in working on campus, should explore the opportunities of Student Hourly Employment (SHE). SHE jobs are university positions available to all students who are currently enrolled as a student. There is no financial need or grade point average requirement. SHE employers will arrange work hours based on need and the students' academic schedules. Student job postings can be found online at: https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com . Select 'Search jobs' option from the menu bar on the left of the screen. For 'Position Type,' select \"Student\" Federal Work Study Federally Work Study is a funded aid program that provides positions to qualifying Ohio University students. Eligibility for this program is based on the results of the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA). For additional information and eligibility requirements, please visit the Student Financial Aid and Scholarships website . PACE (Program to Aid Career Exploration) The Program to Aid Career Exploration (PACE) is an on-campus, internship-like work program is unique to Ohio University. Eligibility for this program is determined by completing the online PACE application. There are credit hour, GPA, and financial need requirements. For additional information and eligibility requirements, please visit the Student Financial Aid and Scholarships website . Looking for additional employment opportunities? Contact Career Services . Eligibility for Retirement Exemption Explore Apply Give Academic Programs Online Degrees Visit Campus Map & Parking Resources Event Calendar Academic Calendar News Libraries Work at OHIO Report a Website Issue Locations Athens Chillicothe Eastern Lancaster Southern Zanesville Contact Human Resources Grosvenor West 103 1 Ohio University Athens, OH 45701 Directions uhr@ohio.edu 740.593.1636 Human Resources ADA Compliance AOHEA Compliance Employment Law Notices FORUM Act Report Mission and Statement of Commitment Notice of Non-Discrimination Privacy Statement State Authorization Title IX Coordinator © 2026 Ohio University . All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.ohio.edu/hr/jobs/dual-careers": {
      "title": "Opportunities for Spouses/Partners",
      "description": "Opportunities for Spouses/Partners | Ohio University Skip to main content Close Search Search within: Human Resources ohio.edu Info for... Info for: Future Students Parents/Families Alumni/Friends Current Students Faculty/Staff Quick Links Log In Catmail Canvas MyOHIO Student Center Library Account Locations Visit Athens Campus Regional Campuses OHIO Online Connect Faculty/Staff Directory Contact Us Apply Give Search Search Menu Human Resources Employee Resources HR Quicklinks My Personal Information Workforce Forms Policies and Notices Employee Perks and Discounts Calendars Employment & Life Changes Hire & Manage Performance Management Hiring & Search Resources Onboarding Tools Employee Lookup Hiring Student Employees Employee Recognition Guide Access PeopleAdmin Labor Relations Labor (Union) Relations Faculty Petition for Representation Collective Bargaining Agreements Seniority Roster Workplace Support Employee Resources for Accessibility HR Business Partners by Planning Unit OHIO FlexWork Benefits Health & Insurance Benefits Benefits Guides Eligibility Premiums Disability Changing & Managing Benefits Retirement & Financial Planning Financial Wellness Preparing to Retire Retirement Plan Options Retirement@Work Supplemental Accounts Educational & Wellness Educational Benefits Worklife and Wellbeing Leave & Time Off Holiday Schedule Sick & Personal Time Vacation Time Leaves Winter Break Closure Compensation & Pay Pay Structures Payroll Schedules Payroll Services Salary Database Total Compensation Estimator OHIO Jobs Job Postings Student Employment Opportunities for Spouses / Partners Professional Development at OHIO Campus and Community Culture Working at OHIO Center For Employee Excellence Professional Development Professional Development Catalog Learning Experiences Helpful Links Info for... Info for: Future Students Parents/Families Alumni/Friends Current Students Faculty/Staff Quick Links Log In Catmail Canvas MyOHIO Student Center Library Account Locations Visit Athens Campus Regional Campuses OHIO Online Connect Faculty/Staff Directory Contact Us Apply Give Search Navigate OHIO About OHIO Admission Athletics Academics Life at OHIO Connect With Us Human Resources Grosvenor West 103 1 Ohio University Athens, OH 45701 Directions uhr@ohio.edu 740.593.1636 Human Resources Breadcrumb OHIO University Human Resources Ohio University Jobs Opportunities for Spouses/Partners Opportunities for Spouses/Partners Site-specific navigation Job Postings Student Employment Retirement Exemption Student Employment Eligibility Student Professional Etiquette Opportunities for Spouses / Partners Professional Development at OHIO Welcome to the Dual Career Network (DCN). Our program is designed to help partners of new employees in networking and locating employment opportunities in the Athens area. By coordinating with several offices on campus, the DCN is committed to providing the support needed to prospective and new faculty, staff, and their families upon arrival at Ohio University. While we are dedicated to providing assistance and building a platform for an effective job search using the services and tools available at Ohio University, we cannot guarantee employment. We look forward to helping you with your job search! Who is eligible to participate? Dual Career Services are available to spouses or benefits-eligible partners of an Ohio University faculty or staff member interested in career opportunities in the surrounding communities as well as Ohio University. The services offered through the Dual Career Network are free and may continue for up to two years. For more information on eligibility, contact the HR Business Partner for your department . Career Resources Some of the Dual Career Network services available through the University are: Consultations. To assess what position is being sought, the spouse/partner will complete an initial consultation. This consultation will provide the Dual Career Network with the information to seek out positions that align with the client’s interest and experience, identify capabilities of an individual well-suited for a particular career, and develop a job search plan. Following this consultation, the DCN will provide further assistance in exploring employment options both within the University and in the Athens community. Resume/Vitae Review. DCN offers review of curriculum vitae, resumes, and cover letters. Ohio University Hiring Support. Upon applying for an Ohio University position, spouses/partners will notify their Human Resources contact, who may forward any pertinent information to the academic administrative units. Additional Services Impact Solutions Employee Assistance and Work/Life Program. Confidential 24/7 live professional assistance. Professional face-to-face counseling. Unlimited telephone guidance, counseling, coaching, and crisis intervention. Provider referral assistance with issues such as: childcare, eldercare, parenting, financial and legal issues, and more Educational Benefits Program. Ohio University provides 100% instructional fee waivers for educational opportunities at the undergraduate and graduate level to faculty, administrative, classified staff, and their spouse/partner and children. How to get Started Complete the Dual Career Network Intake Form . Be prepared to upload your resume or CV when you complete the form. You will be contacted by an HR Business Partner to learn more about the program and to get started. Resources Dual Career Network Intake Form Explore Apply Give Academic Programs Online Degrees Visit Campus Map & Parking Resources Event Calendar Academic Calendar News Libraries Work at OHIO Report a Website Issue Locations Athens Chillicothe Eastern Lancaster Southern Zanesville Contact Human Resources Grosvenor West 103 1 Ohio University Athens, OH 45701 Directions uhr@ohio.edu 740.593.1636 Human Resources ADA Compliance AOHEA Compliance Employment Law Notices FORUM Act Report Mission and Statement of Commitment Notice of Non-Discrimination Privacy Statement State Authorization Title IX Coordinator © 2026 Ohio University . All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "Ohio University: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:www.ohiouniversityjobs.com,2005:/postings/all_jobs Ohio University: All Jobs 2026-03-16T21:28:09-04:00 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56306 2026-03-16T21:28:08-04:00 2026-03-16T21:28:09-04:00 Pool Posting - Instructor, Counseling and Higher Education (non-tenure track) <div>Instructors selected from this pool will teach fully online courses in the Applied Human Services program. Courses focus on foundational knowledge and skills relevant to careers in human services and community support roles.<br><br></div> Counseling and Higher Education 03/16/2026 <div>This rolling application pool will remain open through March 2, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57580 2026-08-28T16:30:26-04:00 2026-08-28T16:30:26-04:00 Administrative Specialist <div>Supports the general administrative functions of a wide variety of academic or administrative units including answering phones, greeting/referring/assisting visitors, customers, staff, or others, preparing documents and reports, compiling records, scheduling meetings, organizing and maintaining information, coordinating calendars, analyzing data including budgetary expenditures, and providing high level administrative assistance to executives.<br><br>Job Responsibilities<br>• May supervise or oversee the work of Technical &amp; Administrative Support staff and/or student employees.<br>• Resolves complex and unique problems that require an ability to interpret established policies and procedures.<br>• Oversees department unit administrative processes.<br>• Coordinates complex processes and initiatives such as grant proposals, contracts /or complex academic processes such as tenure case approvals, faculty searches, complicated course scheduling or sensitive graduate application processes.<br>• Plans and implements projects, special events, and/or programs that require a high level of coordination with multiple constituents and departments.<br>• Composes and edits internal and external correspondence and documents, including such things as manuscript submissions for scientific journals.<br>• Manages academic courses and textbook information. Plans and maintains website as well as other department publications.<br>• Prepares and monitors internal budget and other financial documents for a departmental work unit. Recommends purchases. Reviews and follows up on discrepancies in standard expenditures.</div> LNCSTR Student Services <div>The hourly rate starts at $16.84<a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation-pay/pay-structures/afscme-3200-pay-structure\"><strong>.</strong></a><strong> </strong>The final offer will be commensurate with the candidate’s education and experience in relation to the minimum qualifications for the position. Pay is accompanied by Ohio University’s generous benefits package, which includes:</div><ul><li>Free tuition for employees and dependents</li><li>Comprehensive insurance coverage, including health, prescription, vision, dental, orthodontia, and life insurance</li><li>An excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% employer contribution</li><li>Wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a robust employee assistance program</li><li>Paid parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more</li></ul><div>Additional information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/</strong></a></div> 08/28/2026 <div>Please apply by September 24, 2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57294 2026-07-28T13:42:15-04:00 2026-07-28T13:42:16-04:00 Student IT Support Specialist (CHILLICOTHE CAMPUS) <div>The Ohio University <strong>Chillicothe Campus</strong> invites applications for the position of Student IT Support Specialist. This position will work on the Chillicothe campus which is located in Chillicothe, Ohio. Specific departmental duties may include:<br><br><strong>Help Desk Support</strong></div><div>· Answering the help desk phone, entering work orders, and resolving issues when possible</div><div>· Check out and deliver equipment</div><div>· Assisting with inventory, testing, and cleaning of computer equipment.</div><div>· Supporting campus projects as needed<br><br></div><div><strong>OULN Classroom Operator Support</strong><br> · Responsible to be sure equipment is powered, connected and functioning for class</div><div>· Distribute and collect papers, assignments, etc. before class and return to the proper department/location immediately after class</div><div>· Log any classroom technical issues and relay information to appropriate support team using the Teams application<br><br></div><div><strong>Campus Event Support</strong></div><div>· Setup computer, audio and AV equipment for scheduled campus events</div><div>· Operate equipment during event</div><div>· Troubleshoot any issues and resolve as necessary</div><div>· Return equipment to appropriate storage location(s) when event ends</div><div><br></div> Regional Higher Education <div>$11.00 per hour</div> 07/28/2026 11/30/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56726 2026-05-18T10:41:14-04:00 2026-05-18T10:41:14-04:00 Instructor, Mathematics (Part-time, non-tenure track, POOL POSTING) <div>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions as student demand dictates. The number of courses offered in the Department of Mathematics is largely dependent on student demand; therefore, we often have the need for part-time instructors with very short notice. Such part-time positions will be filled utilizing qualified applicants from this pool.<br><br>Applications will be accepted into the pool through May 2, 2027, and will be utilized to fill positions for the 2026-2027 academic year.<br><br>This instructor position in the Department of Mathematics will consist of teaching up to 3 introductory mathematics courses, but no more than 11 credit hours per semester.</div> Mathematics <div>Pay is set according to college approved rates. Please visit <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/cas/dean/faculty-affairs/summer-overload-guidelines\"><strong>A&amp;S Summer and Overload Course Policy | Ohio University</strong></a> for more information. Pay is accompanied by an excellent retirement plan and paid sick time.</div> 05/18/2026 <div>05/02/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57634 2026-09-04T16:51:32-04:00 2026-09-04T16:51:32-04:00 Assistant Baseball Camp Coach (3 positions) ICA Sports Camps https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56069 2026-02-16T15:22:18-05:00 2026-02-16T15:22:19-05:00 School of Dance Online Instructors (POOL POSTING) <div>This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Summer 2026 and Academic Year 2026-27 in Dance.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Dance to teach online courses as needed.</div> School of Dance 02/16/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57509 2026-08-20T10:54:54-04:00 2026-08-20T10:54:55-04:00 Resident Director Residence Life West Green https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57296 2026-07-28T13:47:44-04:00 2026-07-28T13:47:45-04:00 Student IT Support Specialist (EASTERN CAMPUS) <div>The Ohio University <strong>Eastern Campus</strong> invites applications for the position of Student IT Support Specialist. This position will work on the Eastern campus which is located in St. Clairsville, Ohio. Specific departmental duties may include:<br><br><strong>Help Desk Support</strong></div><div>· Answering the help desk phone, entering work orders, and resolving issues when possible</div><div>· Check out and deliver equipment</div><div>· Assisting with inventory, testing, and cleaning of computer equipment.</div><div>· Supporting campus projects as needed<br><br><br></div><div><strong>OULN Classroom Operator Support</strong><br> · Responsible to be sure equipment is powered, connected and functioning for class</div><div>· Distribute and collect papers, assignments, etc. before class and return to the proper department/location immediately after class</div><div>· Log any classroom technical issues and relay information to appropriate support team using the Teams application<br><br><br></div><div><strong>Campus Event Support</strong></div><div>· Setup computer, audio and AV equipment for scheduled campus events</div><div>· Operate equipment during event</div><div>· Troubleshoot any issues and resolve as necessary</div><div>· Return equipment to appropriate storage location(s) when event ends</div> Regional Higher Education <div>$11.00 per hour</div> 07/28/2026 11/30/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56370 2026-03-24T16:54:31-04:00 2026-03-24T16:54:31-04:00 Adjunct Instructor of Biological Sciences, Beginning Fall Semester 2026 and/or Spring 2027 (POOL POSTING) <div>Ohio University Regional Campuses are seeking part-time instructors to teach <strong>Biological Sciences </strong>courses at the undergraduate level <strong>in-person</strong> at the <strong>Lancaster and Eastern campuses</strong>. The exact number of Instructors needed is undetermined at this time as it is primarily dependent upon enrollments and overall student demand. When a need arises, the department will select qualified candidates from this pool.<br><br></div><div>Preference will be given to applicants who can teach the following <strong>in-person</strong> sections at <strong>Lancaster</strong> and <strong>Eastern</strong>:</div><ul><li>BIOS 1300 (Principles of Human Anatomy and Physiology I)</li><li>BIOS 1310 (Principles of Human Anatomy and Physiology II)</li></ul><div><br><strong>Lancaster- in person:</strong></div><ul><li>BIOS 1030 (Human Biology)</li><li>BIOL 1010 (Principles of Biology, lecture)</li></ul><div><br></div><div>BIOS 1030: For nonmajors. Humans as biological organisms: our origins, ecology, and inheritance, and functioning of our body systems.<br><br>BIOS 1300: Introduction to the structure and function of the human body using chemicals, cells, tissues, to study the integumentary, skeletal, muscular and nervous systems.<br><br></div><div>BIOS 1310: is a continuation of the BIOS 1300 series, the second course in a 2-course introduction to the structure and function of the human body, featuring study and critical-thinking evaluation of the endocrine, cardiovascular, lymphatic &amp; immune, respiratory, gastrointestinal, urinary and reproductive systems.<br><br></div><div>BIOL 1010: Non-science majors explore living organisms from the cellular to ecosystem levels, using scientific information and laboratory exercises to understand historic discovery and contemporary issues in biology and evolutionary processes.<br><br>Position will include teaching from 3 credit hours to up to 11 credit hours per term.</div> Regional Higher Education <div>Standard rates per credit hour. Please visit www.ohio.edu/regional<br>for more information on teaching rates.</div> 03/24/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until October 19, 2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57591 2026-09-01T15:58:16-04:00 2026-09-01T15:58:16-04:00 Assistant Professor of Instruction, Nursing <div>Ohio University School of Nursing is seeking two non-tenure track faculty candidates for traditional on-campus BSN students. These are full-time, 9-month positions at the Assistant Professor of Instruction rank at the Athens campus. The candidates will be responsible to plan, implement, and be responsible for BSN student instruction. Didactic instruction will be assigned based on expertise and credentials. Assigned didactic teaching modalities will be face-to-face. In addition, online class delivery may be assigned as needed, based on expertise and credentials. Successful candidates may be expected to provide clinical site, laboratory, and didactic instruction to BSN student learners for all BSN courses.<br><br>Additional expectations include (but are not limited to):</div><ul><li>Meeting with course faculty to develop course expectations.</li><li>Identifying students' needs in terms of objectives of the relevant course.</li><li>Providing instruction to students at the clinical sites, laboratory/simulation settings, and classroom to acquire professional attitudes, knowledge, and skills.</li><li>Assisting students in using problem-solving techniques.</li></ul><div><br>Successful candidates will be required to be on campus throughout the academic year (August through May).<br><br>Teaching assignments/instructional responsibilities will be based on candidate expertise and/or credentials.<br><br>All School of Nursing faculty members are expected to collaboratively and actively engage in the planning, implementation, and evaluation of student instruction and to participate in School of Nursing governance to ensure program standards and outcomes are fully met.</div> Nursing-Athens <div>The salary for this position is $68,500. Ohio University also offers employees a generous benefits package which includes health benefits and education benefits for employees and eligible dependents.</div> 09/01/2026 <div>Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, please apply by 10/1/2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56781 2026-05-22T16:34:08-04:00 2026-05-22T16:34:09-04:00 School of Nursing Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Zanesville Campus, Beginning Fall 2026  (POOL POSTING) <div>The Ohio University School of Nursing Zanesville Campus seeks adjunct clinical focus faculty candidates with an emphasis on teaching clinical competencies with Associate and Bachelor Degree Nursing students. These positions are term positions and will be filled as needs arise for the Zanesville campus.<br><br>Faculty are expected to plan, implement, and evaluate instruction for student clinical and simulation lab experiences. These individuals will provide instruction, supervision, guidance and counsel to nursing students in relation to ADN and BSN program objectives and includes (1) planning student learning experiences; (2) evaluating student progress; (3) recording and reporting as required by the School of Nursing.<br><br>Clinical sites include the following in the state of Ohio:<br><br>Genesis Hospital (Zanesville, Ohio) (most highly used)<br>Muskingum Valley Health Center (Zanesville, Ohio)<br>Ohio Health Southeastern Medical Center ( Cambridge, Ohio)<br>Licking Hospital (Newark, Ohio)<br>Fairfield Medical (Lancaster, Ohio)<br>Nationwide Children’s (Columbus, Ohio)<br>Community Health sites (Zanesville, Ohio)</div><div>Other: various other facilities may be used for precepted students<br><br></div><div><br>Seeking experience in:<br>Medical Surgical Nursing<br>Behavioral Health<br>Pediatrics<br>Obstetrics<br>Community nursing<br><br>The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.</div> ZNSVL Nursing <div>Hourly rate based on education.</div> 05/22/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until September 15, 2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56071 2026-02-16T15:22:50-05:00 2026-02-16T15:22:50-05:00 School of Film Online Instructor (POOL POSTING) <div>This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Summer 2026 and Academic Year 2026-27 in Film.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities to reach online asynchronous courses in Film.</div> School of Film 02/16/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57523 2026-08-21T13:17:02-04:00 2026-08-21T13:17:02-04:00 Records Management Senior Specialist <div>Oversees file storage and records management. Organizes, converts, and integrates files for storage. Locates and retrieves records as requested.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>Job Responsibilities&nbsp;<br>• Acts as liaison between University, community, and outside federal and private agencies to respond to complex requests for all types of records, information, and data.&nbsp;<br>• Typically supervises and/or leads TAS staff and/or student employees.&nbsp;<br>• Develops and directs processing, maintenance, and daily operations of data and/or records system(s).&nbsp;<br>• Assures security and confidentiality and makes decisions pertinent to records according to University policy, government regulations and/or compliance issues.&nbsp;<br>• Handles requests and coordinates collection of all types of information.&nbsp;<br>• Prepares and distributes special reports and impact studies for administration having direct impact on University (e.g., subsidy, accreditation).&nbsp;<br>• Ensures compliance with governmental regulations and University policies, procedures, and guidelines.&nbsp;<br>• Serves as primary contact for release and protection of confidential and sensitive records.&nbsp;<br>• Develops and implements procedures related to records management.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br><br></div> Registrar's Office <div>Starting pay range $19.38 – $24.70<br><br>Ohio University is proud to offer a robust healthcare plan that includes maternity care, transgender care, counseling and mental healthcare, prescription coverage, vision, dental, orthodontia care, and more. Our robust benefits package also includes paid holidays, sick time, personal time, an instructional fee waiver up to 100% for self and dependents, an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% employer contribution, a 12-week parental leave program, adoption reimbursement, flextime and flexplace policies, an employee assistance program, access to professional development programs, wellbeing incentive programs, and additional employee resources. Additional information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits</strong></a></div> 08/21/2026 <div>09/07/2026</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/53182 2025-04-25T18:58:57-04:00 2025-04-25T18:58:58-04:00 Student Employee - Culinary Services <div><br><br></div> Culinary Services <div>For Culinary Services student employment and to apply go to <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/food/about/student-employment\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/food/about/student-employment</strong></a></div> 09/23/2022 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57323 2026-07-30T11:01:17-04:00 2026-07-30T11:01:18-04:00 Instructor, OMM, Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine (AY 26-27 Pool Posting) Periodic Engagement Role <div>The Ohio University Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine (OU-HCOM) is seeking Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) physicians for in-person, faculty teaching positions across the state of Ohio. Positions can include regular but low frequency teaching for medical students in their first two years of medical school on one of our three campuses in Athens, Cleveland, or Dublin, Ohio, and/or small group instruction sessions one to four times per month over seven months for medical students in years three and four at various clinical sites across the state of Ohio. <br><br>Successful applicants will have special interest and qualifications in the practice and teaching of osteopathic principles and manipulative medicine, possess a strong desire to teach and advise osteopathic medical students within the curriculum, and strong interpersonal skills to relate to diverse faculty, staff, students and community members. Applications for these positions will be reviewed for consideration if/when a need arises.<br><br><strong>RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong><br><br>Teach the clinical application of osteopathic principles and manipulative medicine in ambulatory and hospital-based practices.<br><br></div><div><strong>Small Group Instruction for Years 3 and 4:</strong><br><br></div><ul><li>Teach OMM skills in 7 sessions between August and April at an assigned clinical site near you</li><li>Each small group session is 2 hours and roughly every 4 weeks excluding the months of January, May, June, and July</li><li>Utilize provided materials (PowerPoints with demonstrations of each technique)</li><li>Provide clinical correlations, modifications of techniques, additional techniques and clinical skills, and/or other activities to individualize sessions</li><li>Evaluate students’ mastery of the required techniques</li></ul><div><br><strong>Clinical Instruction for Years 1 and 2:</strong><br><br></div><ul><li>Team-teach courses assigned to the Department of Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) on one of our three campuses in Athens, Cleveland or Dublin, Ohio</li><li>Participate in ongoing programs and program development of the Department of OMM including pre- and post-medical school training and other scholarly activities as appropriate</li></ul><div><br><strong>About the Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine:</strong></div><div><br><strong>Mission:</strong></div><div>We pride ourselves on our strong focus on our mission: training osteopathic primary care physicians to serve Ohio.</div><div>Our medical school educates physicians committed to practice in Ohio, emphasizes primary care, engages in focused research, and embraces both Appalachian and urban communities. Integral to this mission, our college community commits itself to: providing a clinically integrated, learning-centered, osteopathic medical education continuum for students, interns, residents and primary care associates; embracing public service; and improving the health and well-being of underserved populations.</div><div><br><strong>Vision:</strong></div><div>A healthier Ohio, empowered by compassionate osteopathic physicians.</div><div>With our graduates and partners, we advance care and knowledge to improve the health of our communities. Our culture is built upon resiliency, courage and compassion. Our physicians humanize each patient encounter, bridging the gap between therapeutics, medical technologies, health systems, care delivery and disparity.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Essential Values:</strong></div><div>These fundamental principles form the foundation of the culture at our college: wholeness and balance within each person; integrity; community of mutual respect; acceptance of others; pursuit of excellence; a climate of scholarship; and commitment to service, generosity and compassion.</div><div><br><strong>Our Campuses:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses</strong></a></div><div><br><strong>Why Choose Ohio University?</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/jobs/working-ohio\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/jobs/working-ohio</strong></a></div><div><a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/community-health\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/community-health</strong></a></div><div><a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits</strong></a></div> HCOM - Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) <div>Pay is commensurate with education and experience, while also considering internal equity and is accompanied by an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% company contribution, paid sick leave, and access to professional development programs. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/.</strong></a></div> 07/30/2026 <div>6/30/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56417 2026-04-01T00:09:32-04:00 2026-04-01T00:09:33-04:00 Open Rank Tenure Track Faculty (Clinical Child Psychology Focus) <div>The Department of Psychology at Ohio University invites applicants for <strong>an open-rank tenure-track</strong> faculty position within the <strong>Clinical Child Psychology Area</strong> of our American Psychological Association-accredited clinical psychology Ph.D. training program. This position will begin on August 16, 2027, with the possibility of an earlier start date of January 1, 2027. Preference will be given to applicants whose program of research would create synergies with faculty in the department. Incoming faculty will have the opportunity to join the Center for Intervention Research in Schools.</div><div><br>Ohio University is a Carnegie Foundation R1 (highest research activity) institution, and the successful applicant will demonstrate a strong research record. Our clinical program follows the scientist-practitioner model of training and maintains an on-site training clinic that provides ample opportunities for clinical practice and research. Reflecting the department’s commitment to collaborative, cross-disciplinary scholarship, research specialties often cut across both the experimental and clinical psychology programs. Multiple resources for developing and maintaining a strong research program are available, including infrastructure for grant procurement, grant mentoring, research lab space, start-up funds, and support for graduate students (stipends, tuition waivers, travel support).</div><div><br>Responsibilities include maintaining an active, high-quality, fundable research program, directing graduate student research, teaching graduate and undergraduate courses, supervising assessment and/or therapy practica, and participating in departmental service. Teaching load is typically 1-2 courses each semester during the 9-month academic calendar, depending on research productivity. Candidates must be committed to working effectively with students, faculty and staff who hold diverse perspectives.</div><div><br>Ohio University has a rich history and beautiful Appalachian settings. As part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. Athens, home of Ohio University, provides a classic and vibrant residential learning environment for over 30,000 students, and is a family-friendly and culturally rich community. The charm of treelined brick walkways on the University’s College Green makes you feel as if you are at a small college rather than a large university. Athens is frequently cited as one of the best college towns, including by USA Today and World Atlas.</div><div><br>The Department of Psychology is home to 33 full-time faculty who serve over 1,400 undergraduate students and 60 graduate students across the main and seven regional campuses in Southern and Central Ohio. Committed to excellence in research, teaching, and service, the department is consistently recognized as one of the top departments at Ohio University for its outstanding research and student engagement. The clinical psychology program is within the College of Arts &amp; Sciences and is central to Ohio University’s transformative learning experience.</div> Psychology <div>Salary is commensurate with experience and credentials and is accompanied by our generous university benefits such as tuition for self and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan including company contributions, parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional Information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/</strong></a>.</div> 04/01/2026 <div>09/15/2026</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57595 2026-09-02T08:49:24-04:00 2026-09-02T08:49:24-04:00 Student Leader Culinary Services Staff <div>While working as a student leader in Culinary Services customer service and safety are top priorities. By taking on this postion it is an opportunity to grow and enhance your leadership capabilites. It is important to have the ability to lead&nbsp; communicate and with other student empoyees, student coordinators, and management while also representing Culinary Services as a whole.</div> Culinary Services - Shively <div>level 4 $14/hour</div> 09/03/2026 09/11/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56807 2026-05-28T14:44:52-04:00 2026-05-28T14:44:52-04:00 Part-time Instructor - Social Work (POOL POSTING) <div>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions on the<strong> Athens campus</strong> as student demand dictates. The number of Social Work courses offered each semester is largely dependent on student demand. Therefore, we often have the need for part-time instructors with very short notice. Such part-time positions will be filled utilizing qualified applicants from this pool. Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis to teach practice or field courses. Instruct classes at the Graduate or Undergraduate level for Athens campus and/or online (e-campus).</div> Social Work 05/28/2026 <div>02/16/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56073 2026-02-16T15:23:26-05:00 2026-02-16T15:23:27-05:00 Interior Architecture Instructor - Athens Campus, School of Art + Design (Pool Posting) <div>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions for delivering in-person courses at the Athens Campus in our Interior Architecture Department during the 2026/2027 academic year.<br><br></div> Art 02/16/2026 <div>Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57527 2026-08-21T14:01:56-04:00 2026-08-21T14:01:57-04:00 Success Advisor Provost Office https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/53492 2025-05-20T12:09:35-04:00 2025-05-20T12:09:35-04:00 School of Nursing Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Zanesville Campus, Beginning Academic Year 2025-26 (POOL POSTING) <div>The Ohio University School of Nursing Zanesville Campus seeks adjunct clinical focus faculty candidates with an emphasis on teaching clinical competencies with Associate and Bachelor Degree Nursing students. These positions are term positions and will be filled as needs arise for the Zanesville campus.<br><br>Faculty are expected to plan, implement, and evaluate instruction for student clinical and simulation lab experiences. These individuals will provide instruction, supervision, guidance and counsel to nursing students in relation to ADN and BSN program objectives and includes (1) planning student learning experiences; (2) evaluating student progress; (3) recording and reporting as required by the School of Nursing.<br><br>Clinical sites include the following in the state of Ohio:<br><br>Genesis Hospital (Zanesville, Ohio) (most highly used)<br>Muskingum Valley Health Center (Zanesville, Ohio)<br>Ohio Health Southeastern Medical Center ( Cambridge, Ohio)<br>Licking Hospital (Newark, Ohio)<br>Fairfield Medical (Lancaster, Ohio)<br>Nationwide Children’s (Columbus, Ohio)<br>Community Health sites (Zanesville, Ohio)</div><div>Other: various other facilities may be used for precepted students<br><br></div><div><br>Seeking experience in:<br>Medical Surgical Nursing<br>Behavioral Health<br>Pediatrics<br>Obstetrics<br>Community nursing<br><br>The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.</div> ZNSVL Nursing <div>Compensation is an hourly rate commensurate on highest achieved nursing degree.</div> 05/19/2025 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until May 31, 2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57392 2026-08-07T11:30:39-04:00 2026-08-07T11:30:40-04:00 Educational Research and Evaluation Instructor POOL POSTING <div>The Department of Educational Studies in Ohio University’s Patton College of Education invites nominations and applications for an adjunct instructor pool within the department of Educational Studies. Applications should be sent to noted link above. Nominations may be sent to Educational Studies department chair, Dr. Jesse Strycker (strycker@ohio.edu). Nominees will then be requested to complete the application process<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate(s) will be assigned a course(s) to teach in Educational Research and Evaluation, offering doctoral and master’s degree programs and an online certificate in mixed methods research.<br><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities:&nbsp;</strong></div><div>The successful candidate(s) may be assigned to teach graduate students on the Athens campus and/or online.</div> Educational Studies 08/07/2026 <div>Please apply by 08/09/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56453 2026-04-06T15:28:45-04:00 2026-04-06T15:28:46-04:00 School of Nursing Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Eastern Campus, Beginning Fall Semester 2026 ( POOL POSTING) <div>The Ohio University School of Nursing Eastern Campus seeks adjunct clinical focus faculty candidates with an emphasis on teaching clinical competencies with bachelor’s degree nursing students. These positions are term positions and will be filled as needs arise for the Eastern campus. Faculty are expected to plan, implement, and evaluate instruction for student clinical and simulation lab experiences. These individuals will provide instruction, supervision, guidance and counsel to nursing students in relation to BSN program objectives and includes (1) planning student learning experiences; (2) evaluating student progress; (3) recording and reporting as required by the School of Nursing.<br><br>Clinical sites are located in the following areas:<br>Barnesville, OH<br>Bellaire, OH<br>Belmont, OH<br>Cambridge, OH<br>Martins Ferry, OH<br>Shadyside, OH<br>Steubenville, OH<br>St. Clairsville, OH<br>Glen Dale, WV<br>Wheeling, WV<br><br>Seeking experience in:<br>Obstetrics<br>Pediatrics<br>Mental Health<br>Medical Surgical<br><br>The need for these positions is undetermined currently and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.</div> ESTRN Nursing <div>Hourly rate based on education.</div> 04/06/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until September 15, 2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57600 2026-09-02T11:15:05-04:00 2026-09-02T11:15:06-04:00 Executive Director, Kennedy Museum of Art (One Year) Kennedy Museum Of Art https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57535 2026-08-22T18:18:07-04:00 2026-08-22T18:18:08-04:00 Assistant Professor of Instruction, Child Development Center (Teacher) <div>Context: The Patton College has four Core Values: 1) Preparing ethical and reflective leader-educators and human service professionals, 2) Lifelong learning, 3) Change agency and 4) Diversity. At its core, the College is committed to serving a diverse student population that includes international and non-traditional students and to providing service to the region through professional engagement and collaboration. We are looking for candidates that will contribute to these goals, bring a strong commitment to teaching, and will work with colleagues within the College and Child Development Center to improve education.<br><br></div><div><strong>The Assistant Professor of Instruction is a Teacher in a classroom at the Child Development Center. They have responsibility of the classroom, coordinating activities and planning for children while working with an assistant teacher and mentoring Teacher Candidates.</strong><br><br></div><div>Responsibilities:<br><br></div><ul><li>Teach and supervise young children from diverse backgrounds through planning, implementing, and reflecting on daily experiences alongside teaching team</li><li>Interact with everyone with kindness, warmth, and an assets based perspective</li><li>Use observational assessments, knowledge of child development, creativity, reflection, weekly classroom planning meetings and family input to develop emergent curriculum in the classroom</li><li>Provide a safe, clean, organized, warm, stimulating classroom environment</li><li>Assist children working through developmental skills and build classroom community</li><li>Use Brigance screen two times each year with each child</li><li>Follow the State of Ohio Early Learning and Development Standards</li><li>Follow all DCY licensing rules, maintain attendance, tracking sheets, child portfolios, and classroom NAEYC portfolio</li><li>Create Experience Journals and Documentation to make children’s learning visible using digital and paper formats</li><li>Work with small groups and individual children while supervising the whole group.</li><li>Able to prioritize and make appropriate quick decisions</li><li>Develop strong relationships with families, encourage frequent/daily communication, meet with families at least twice a year and submit written conference reports</li><li>Supervise, support, and assess sophomore Teacher Candidates with diverse backgrounds in the classroom daily</li><li>Participate in the Center community, staff meetings and professional development days</li><li>Attend and participate in Reggio Study Group Meetings, is a continual learner, and shares own learning or that of the children with others.</li><li>Reflective and able to recognize one’s successes and areas for growth</li></ul> Child Development Center 08/22/2026 <div>The position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by September 13, 2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56973 2026-06-22T15:05:59-04:00 2026-06-22T15:06:00-04:00 School of Nursing - Athens Campus - BSN Fixed-Term Instructor, Academic Year 2026-2027 (Pool) <div>Ohio University School of Nursing BSN program on the Athens, OH campus is seeking applications for individuals to serve as adjunct (part-time) faculty in various capacities as need arises for the 2026-2027 academic year (August - May). This includes, but is not limited to, clinical instructors and lab instructors. These individuals will provide instruction, supervision, guidance and counsel to undergraduate nursing students in relation to BSN program objectives and includes (1) planning and supervising student learning experiences; (2) evaluating student progress; (3) recording and reporting as required by the School of Nursing.<br><br>These positions will have responsibilities that require the successful candidates to be on campus in Athens, OH or on site at clinical placement facilities located in southeast OH, central OH, and/or western WV. These positions are NOT remote teaching positions.<br><br>Those who are hired as adjunct instructors for clinical supervision of students must agree to meet the requirements of the assigned clinical facility, including, but not limited to, proof of compliance for up-to-date immunizations/vaccines, clear FBI and BCI background checks, drug screen testing, meeting lifting requirements essential for standard nursing duties (approx. 50 lbs.).<br><br>The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.</div> Nursing-Athens <div>Compensation is an hourly rate commensurate on highest achieved nursing degree.</div> 04/30/2026 <div>05/31/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56075 2026-02-16T15:24:21-05:00 2026-02-16T15:24:22-05:00 Graphic Design Instructor - Athens Campus, School of Art + Design  (POOL POSTING) <div>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions for delivering in-person courses at the Athens Campus for our Graphic Design Department during the 2026/2027 academic year.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Art + Design.</div> Art 02/16/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/55646 2025-11-12T10:36:07-05:00 2025-11-12T10:36:07-05:00 Undergraduate Student Assistant, Office of Student Services <div>The Undergraduate Student Assistant serves as the first point of contact for the Office of Student Services. This position provides general office and customer service support, assisting students, faculty, staff, and visitors in a professional and welcoming manner. The ideal candidate will demonstrate strong communication skills, attention to detail, and the ability to maintain confidentiality while working in a fast-paced environment.<br><br><strong>Primary Responsibilities:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Greet and assist students, visitors, and staff in person, by phone, and via email</li><li>Answer general questions related to campus resources, events, and services</li><li>Direct inquiries to appropriate staff members or departments</li><li>Schedule appointments and maintain office calendars as needed</li><li>File, scan, and organize documents; assist with mail and deliveries</li><li>Help prepare materials for orientations, events, and workshops</li><li>Update and maintain bulletin boards and information displays</li><li>Assist with data entry, record keeping, and other clerical duties</li><li>Assist with Enrollment Management, Testing Services, and Student Engagement activities as needed</li><li>Support special projects and campus events coordinated through Student Services; and other duties as assigned</li><li>Maintain a clean and organized front office environment</li><li>Cross-trained in all operations of the Office of Student Services</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Required Qualifications:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Must be a currently enrolled Ohio University student in good academic standing</li><li>Strong interpersonal and communication skills</li><li>Dependable, punctual, and professional in appearance and conduct</li><li>Ability to handle confidential information appropriately</li><li>Basic computer skills (Microsoft Office, Outlook, Teams, etc.)</li><li>Ability to work independently and as part of a team</li></ul><div><br></div> STHRN Administrative Support <div>Hourly rate based on university student employment pay scale.</div> 11/12/2025 12/12/2027 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57423 2026-08-12T11:51:57-04:00 2026-08-12T11:51:57-04:00 Certified Flight Instructor 1 (Pool Posting) Aviation https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56468 2026-04-08T13:47:51-04:00 2026-04-08T13:47:52-04:00 School of Nursing Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Southern Campus, Beginning Fall 2026 (POOL POSTING) <div>The Ohio University School of Nursing Southern Campus seeks adjunct clinical focus faculty candidates with an emphasis on teaching clinical competencies with Associate and Bachelor Degree Nursing students. These positions are term positions and will be filled as needs arise for the Southern campus.<br><br>Faculty are expected to plan, implement, and evaluate instruction for student clinical and lab experiences. These individuals will provide instruction, supervision, guidance, and counsel to nursing students in collaboration with and under the direction of the course lead(s) in relation to nursing program objectives and will include (1) planning student learning experiences; (2) evaluating student progress; (3) recording and reporting as required by the School of Nursing.<br><br>Clinical sites are located in the following areas:<br>Ashland, KY<br>Portsmouth, OH<br>Ironton, OH<br>Huntington, WV<br><br>Seeking experience in: Medical-Surgical Nursing Pediatric Nursing Community Nursing Obstetric Nursing Mental Health Nursing<br><br>The need for these positions is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.</div> STHRN Nursing <div>Hourly based on level of education.</div> 04/08/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until September 15, 2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57610 2026-09-02T15:21:14-04:00 2026-09-02T15:21:14-04:00 Director of Finance OHIO Business Service Center https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56099 2026-02-18T13:22:34-05:00 2026-02-18T13:22:35-05:00 Foundation Program Instructor - Asynchronous Online Program, School of Art + Design (POOL POSTING) <div>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions delivering asynchronous online courses in our Studio Art Foundations Program during the 2026/2027 academic year.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Art + Design.</div> Art 02/18/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57552 2026-08-27T11:25:58-04:00 2026-08-27T11:25:59-04:00 Manager, Zone Maintenance Zone Maintenance https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57064 2026-07-01T10:16:08-04:00 2026-07-01T10:16:08-04:00 Physician Instructor, Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine, part-time, non tenure-track, (Athens, Cleveland, or Dublin Ohio) (AY 26-27 Pool Posting) Periodic Engagement Role <div><strong>About the </strong><a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/\"><strong>Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine</strong></a><strong>:</strong></div><div><br><strong>Mission:</strong><br>We pride ourselves on our strong focus on our mission: training osteopathic primary care physicians to serve Ohio.</div><div>Our medical school educates physicians committed to practice in Ohio, emphasizes primary care, engages in focused research, and embraces both Appalachian and urban communities. Integral to this mission, our college community commits itself to: providing a clinically integrated, learning-centered, osteopathic medical education continuum for students, interns, residents and primary care associates; embracing public service; and improving the health and well-being of underserved populations.</div><div><br><strong>Vision:</strong><br>A healthier Ohio, empowered by compassionate osteopathic physicians.</div><div>With our graduates and partners, we advance care and knowledge to improve the health of our communities. Our culture is built upon resiliency, courage and compassion. Our physicians humanize each patient encounter, bridging the gap between therapeutics, medical technologies, health systems, care delivery and disparity.</div><div><br><strong>Essential Values:</strong><br> These fundamental principles form the foundation of the culture at our college: wholeness and balance within each person; integrity; community of mutual respect; acceptance of others; pursuit of excellence; a climate of scholarship; and commitment to service, generosity and compassion. <br> <br> <strong>Our Campuses:</strong><br> <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses</strong></a><br> <br> <strong>HCOM Admissions:</strong><br> <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-admissions\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-admissions<br></strong></a><br></div><div><strong>Position Description:</strong><br>Physician instructors participate in the delivery of our integrated <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-education/osteopathic-medicine\"><strong>medical curriculum</strong></a> at any one of our three campuses on an as-needed basis. Instructors prepare and perform didactic instruction for and evaluation of osteopathic medical students, including small group teaching and clinical skills laboratory sessions, and/or serve as a clinical content expert/facilitator in the <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-education/osteopathic-medicine\"><strong>Pathway to Health and Wellness Curriculum</strong></a>.</div> HCOM - Executive Dean's Office <div>Pay is commensurate with education and experience, while also considering internal equity and is accompanied by an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% company contribution, paid sick leave, and access to professional development programs. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/.</strong></a></div> 07/01/2026 <div>6/30/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/55667 2025-11-14T15:15:45-05:00 2025-11-14T15:15:46-05:00 Instructor, Pharmacy, Adjunct, Non Tenure Track, (POOL POSTING) <div><strong>Position Description:</strong></div><div><br>The Heritage College is seeking applications for adjunct <strong><em>Instructors</em></strong> <strong><em>of Pharmacy </em></strong>to participate in the delivery of our integrated <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-education/osteopathic-medicine\"><strong>medical curriculum</strong></a> on our Athens, Cleveland, or Dublin, Ohio Campuses on an as needed basis. Selected instructors will join a diverse group of faculty in the <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/departments/family\"><strong>Department of Primary Care</strong></a>, allowing the opportunity to gain training and expertise in additional disciplines.<br><br></div><div><strong>Potential Primary Responsibilities (on an as needed basis):</strong></div><div>· Teach pharmacology content in an integrative team-based teaching and learning environment, including which includes large group interactive learning sessions</div><div>· Collaborate closely with faculty members across the three Heritage College campuses to develop and lead curricular content (i.e., learning objectives, team-based learning sessions, resources, assessments) in a timely manner</div><div>· Participate in small group coaching and mentoring of osteopathic medical students</div><div>· Provide service to the college such as interviewing prospective candidates for admissions to the Heritage College, participating in college-planned outreach activities, serving as faculty representative to a student organization(s), etc.</div><div><br><strong>About the Ohio University Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine</strong></div><div><br><strong>Mission</strong><br> We pride ourselves on our strong focus on our mission: training osteopathic primary care physicians to serve Ohio. Our medical school educates physicians committed to practice in Ohio, emphasizes primary care, engages in focused research, and embraces both Appalachian and urban communities. Integral to this mission, our college community commits itself to: provide a clinically integrated, learning-centered, osteopathic medical education continuum for students, interns, residents and primary care associates.<br><br></div><div><strong>Vision</strong><br> The Heritage College is recognized as the national leader in training osteopathic primary care physicians and the number one producer of primary care physicians in the country.<br><br></div><div><strong>Essential Values</strong><br> These fundamental principles form the foundation of the culture at our college: wholeness and balance within each person; integrity; community of mutual respect; acceptance of others; pursuit of excellence; a climate of scholarship; and commitment to service, generosity and compassion.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Our Campuses:</strong><br> <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses<br><br></strong></a><strong>HCOM Admissions:</strong><br> <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-admissions\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-admissions</strong></a></div> HCOM - Primary Care <div>Pay is commensurate with education and experience, while also considering internal equity and is accompanied by an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% company contribution, paid sick leave, and access to professional development programs. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/.</strong></a></div> 11/14/2025 <div>06/30/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57440 2026-08-13T15:17:22-04:00 2026-08-13T15:17:22-04:00 Music Instructors (POOL POSTING) <div>This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Summer 2026 and Academic Year 2026-27 in Music.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in the following discipline: Music.</div> School of Music 02/19/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56715 2026-05-18T10:04:59-04:00 2026-05-18T10:04:59-04:00 Instructor (part-time) College of Business Graduate & Professional Programs Academic year 2026-2027 (POOL) <div>We are accepting resumes for potential openings in the College of Business Graduate &amp; Professional Programs for Summer 2026 the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.<br><br>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track instructor positions for courses offered by the College of Business as departmental/student demand dictates. Courses may be offered in person on the Athens or Dublin campus, or online.<br><br>The number of courses offered each semester by the College of Business is largely dependent on full-time faculty leave of absences and student demand. Therefore, we often have the need for part-time instructors with very short notice. Such part-time positions will be filled utilizing qualified applicants from this pool.<br><br>When applying, applicants must specify qualifications / interest for specific disciplines and courses. Disciplines include: Accounting, Finance, Analytics Information Systems, Management, Marketing, and Sports Administration. Course descriptions for graduate courses can be found online at <a href=\"https://catalogs.ohio.edu/\"><strong>https://catalogs.ohio.edu/</strong></a>.<br><br>Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis.<br><br><strong>Our Mission at the College of Business</strong><br>We inspire innovators who strategically create value and motivate leaders who serve with grit and determination. We also nurture self-aware citizens who better the world of business.<br><br><strong>About Ohio University</strong><br>Ohio University strives to be the best student-centered, transformative learning community in America, where approximately 30,000 students realize their promise, faculty advance knowledge, staff achieve excellence, and alumni become global leaders. Our Athens Campus offers students a vibrant residential learning experience in one of the nation’s most picturesque academic settings. Additional campuses and centers serve students across the state, and online programs further advance the University’s commitment to providing educational access and opportunity.</div> Business Graduate & Professional Programs 05/18/2026 <div>04/14/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57618 2026-09-03T16:44:20-04:00 2026-09-03T16:44:21-04:00 Accounts and Operations Manager VP For Research https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56116 2026-02-19T14:23:33-05:00 2026-02-19T14:23:33-05:00 Theater Instructors (POOL POSTING) <div>This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Summer 2026 and Academic Year 2026-27 in Theater.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Theater.</div> School of Theater 02/19/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57559 2026-08-27T13:17:56-04:00 2026-08-27T13:17:56-04:00 Parking Field Operations Manager Transportation & Parking https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57161 2026-07-13T14:18:07-04:00 2026-07-13T14:18:08-04:00 Extended Police Officer Pool Posting <div>Under general supervision, patrols grounds and buildings to protect lives and property, prevent crimes and enforce laws, investigate crimes. Carries firearms and/or makes arrests and testifies in court. Makes police presentations to groups and organizations.</div> Ohio University Police Department <div>Current pay for uncertified recruits while attending basic academy training is $23.76&nbsp; . Current starting pay for certified police officers ranges from $27.95 - $40.92, depending on education and experience. <strong>NEW HIRES ELIGIBLE FOR SIGNING BONUS OF $5,000.</strong></div> 07/19/2022 <div>07/31/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57627 2026-09-04T12:06:32-04:00 2026-09-04T12:06:33-04:00 Assistant Director, Alumni Success Alumni Relations https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/55837 2026-01-07T10:37:08-05:00 2026-01-07T10:37:08-05:00 Instructor, Biomedical Sciences (part-time, non-tenure track, POOL POSTING) Campus of Choice <div>Instructors are needed to teach in the areas of human anatomy, physiology, histology and/or other general biomedical science related specialties in the Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine. Teaching workload can include but is not limited to classroom group learning activities (preparing teaching objectives, reading lists, learning assessments, creating pre-recorded tutorials and problem sets, group facilitation and coaching and laboratory teaching). Teaching needs can occur during fall or spring semesters as well as during summer programs (including the post-baccalaureate program, summer scholars program, and the Rural and Underserved Program).</div> HCOM - Biomedical Sciences <div>Pay is commensurate with education and experience, while also considering internal equity and is accompanied by an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% company contribution, paid sick leave, and access to professional development programs. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/.</strong></a></div> 01/07/2026 <div>1/7/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57466 2026-08-17T10:49:14-04:00 2026-08-17T10:49:14-04:00 Admissions Advisor Online, Transfer and Credit Services Center https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56717 2026-05-18T10:15:29-04:00 2026-05-18T10:15:29-04:00 Instructor (part-time) College of Business, Management, Academic year 2026-2027 (POOL) <div>We are accepting resumes for potential openings in the College of Business, Management department for the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.<br><br>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track instructor positions for courses offered by the College of Business on the Athens campus as departmental/student demand dictates.<br><br>The number of courses offered each semester by the College of Business is largely dependent on full-time faculty leave of absences and student demand. Therefore, we often have the need for part-time instructors with very short notice. Such part-time positions will be filled utilizing qualified applicants from this pool.<br><br>When applying, applicants should specify qualifications / interest for specific disciplines and courses. Course descriptions for undergraduate courses can be found online at <a href=\"https://catalogs.ohio.edu/\"><strong>https://catalogs.ohio.edu/</strong></a>.<br><br>Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis.<br><br><strong>Our Mission at the College of Business</strong><br>We inspire innovators who strategically create value and motivate leaders who serve with grit and determination. We also nurture self-aware citizens who better the world of business.<br><br><strong>About Ohio University</strong><br>Ohio University strives to be the best student-centered, transformative learning community in America, where approximately 30,000 students realize their promise, faculty advance knowledge, staff achieve excellence, and alumni become global leaders. Our Athens Campus offers students a vibrant residential learning experience in one of the nation’s most picturesque academic settings. Additional campuses and centers serve students across the state, and online programs further advance the University’s commitment to providing educational access and opportunity.</div> Management 05/18/2026 <div>4/14/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56118 2026-02-19T14:26:45-05:00 2026-02-19T14:26:46-05:00 Studio Art Instructor - Athens Campus, School of Art + Design (POOL POSTING) <div>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions for delivering in-person courses at the Athens Campus for our undergraduate and/or graduate programs in the following studio art Areas: Ceramics, Digital Art + Technology, Painting + Drawing, Printmaking, Photography + Integrated Media, and Sculpture + Expanded Practice during the 2026/2027 academic year.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Art + Design.</div> Art 02/19/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57567 2026-08-27T16:00:16-04:00 2026-08-27T16:00:16-04:00 Administrative Services Associate <div>Supports the general administrative functions of a wide variety of academic or administrative units including answering phones, greeting/referring/assisting visitors, customers, staff, or others, preparing documents and reports, compiling records, scheduling meetings, organizing and maintaining information, coordinating calendars, analyzing data including budgetary expenditures, and providing high level administrative assistance to executives.<br><br>Job Responsibilities:<br>•May supervise or oversee the work of student employees.<br>•Represents an office as administrative liaison. Responds to non-routine inquiries requiring technical and/or University or unit knowledge.<br>•Utilizes department and/or University policies, practices, and procedures to answer questions and resolve problems and issues.<br>•Coordinates special events that require judgment in determining and prioritizing activities to meet desired results.<br>•Coordinates complex appointments, meetings, and travel itineraries. Triages scheduling issues.<br>•Edits documents and presentations. Composes basic correspondence. Types and coordinates class materials.<br>•Performs a variety of administrative duties regarding academic class scheduling and/or student academic records and/or reports. Duties may include activities such as updating student records, registering students in courses, entering courses into PeopleSoft and assigning classrooms.<br>•Coordinates mass mailing and/or email distribution.<br>•Creates and oversees departmental files, databases, and reports.<br>•Maintains office and/or laboratory supplies and inventory.<br>•Maintains website.<br>•Sets up accounts, tracks budgets, reconciles accounting statements, and follows up on discrepancies. Prepares purchasing and accounting forms for approval. Processes expenses.<br><br><br><br></div> LNCSTR Student Services <div>The hourly rate starts at $14.65<a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation-pay/pay-structures/afscme-3200-pay-structure\"><strong>.</strong></a><strong> </strong>The final offer will be commensurate with the candidate’s education and experience in relation to the minimum qualifications for the position. Pay is accompanied by Ohio University’s generous benefits package, which includes:</div><ul><li>Free tuition for employees and dependents</li><li>Comprehensive insurance coverage, including health, prescription, vision, dental, orthodontia, and life insurance</li><li>An excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% employer contribution</li><li>Wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a robust employee assistance program</li><li>Paid parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more</li></ul><div>Additional information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/</strong></a></div> 08/27/2026 <div>Please apply by September 24, 2026.&nbsp;</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57267 2026-07-24T11:22:23-04:00 2026-07-24T11:22:23-04:00 (POOL) Adjunct Instructor of American Sign Language (non-tenure track) <div>We are accepting applications for adjunct instructors for potential openings for courses in American Sign Language in the Department of Hearing, Speech and Language Sciences for fall and spring semesters of Academic Year (AY) 2026-2027.<del><br><br></del>Applications to this pool will be considered to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions at the Athens campus. The teaching workload will vary based on departmental teaching needs each semester.<br><br>When a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.<br><br>For full consideration for AY 2026-2027 fall semester please apply by Aug 1, 2026.<br><br>For full consideration for AY 2026-2027 spring semester, apply by Dec 15, 2026.<br><br></div> Hearing, Speech and Language Sciences 07/23/2026 <div>06/15/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56719 2026-05-18T10:23:33-04:00 2026-05-18T10:23:33-04:00 Instructor (part-time) College of Business AIS Academic year 2026-2027 (POOL) <div>We are accepting resumes for potential openings in the College of Business Analytics &amp; Information Systems (AIS) department for summer 2026 and the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.<br><br>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track instructor positions for courses offered by the College of Business on the Athens campus as departmental/student demand dictates.<br><br>The number of courses offered each semester by the College of Business is largely dependent on full-time faculty leave of absences and student demand. Therefore, we often have the need for part-time instructors with very short notice. Such part-time positions will be filled utilizing qualified applicants from this pool.<br><br>When applying, applicants should specify qualifications / interest for specific disciplines and courses. Course descriptions for undergraduate courses can be found online at https://catalogs.ohio.edu/.<br><br>Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis.<br><br><strong>Our Mission at the College of Business</strong><br>We inspire innovators who strategically create value and motivate leaders who serve with grit and determination. We also nurture self-aware citizens who better the world of business.<br><br><strong>About Ohio University</strong><br>Ohio University strives to be the best student-centered, transformative learning community in America, where approximately 30,000 students realize their promise, faculty advance knowledge, staff achieve excellence, and alumni become global leaders. Our Athens Campus offers students a vibrant residential learning experience in one of the nation’s most picturesque academic settings. Additional campuses and centers serve students across the state, and online programs further advance the University’s commitment to providing educational access and opportunity.</div> Analytics & Information Systems 05/18/2026 <div>4/14/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57629 2026-09-04T13:26:36-04:00 2026-09-04T13:26:36-04:00 Professor, Mathematics, David N. Keck Chair in Applied Analysis (Tenure Track) <div>The Department of Mathematics at Ohio University seeks applicants for the endowed David N. Keck Chair in Applied Analysis, at the rank of (full) Professor with tenure, to increase the national prominence of the college and university in this academic area. The Chair will <br>• Guide the newly established David N. Keck Center for Applied Mathematics,<br>• Conduct scholarly research,<br>• Share knowledge with our university communities,<br>• Mentor students at all levels, including directing doctoral dissertations and supervising postdoctoral researchers, <br>• Teach undergraduate and graduate courses, and<br>• Participate in the general activities of the department.<br><br>The Chair filling this position should be well placed at the intersection of applied mathematics and analysis, especially in the development and application of differential and integral equations, dynamical systems, probability theory and stochastic processes, numerical analysis and other areas rooted in the general area of analysis. The endowment will provide core benefits to the Chair of:<br>• A salary enhancement,<br>• A reduction in scheduled teaching, and<br>• Funds for travel, registrations, software, materials, visitors, publication charges, hourly undergraduate research assistants, etc.<br><br>The David N. Keck Center for Applied Mathematics was established to advance research, teaching, and innovation in the field of applied mathematics by supporting faculty excellence, student development, and scholarly collaboration. In addition to the endowed Chair, the Center is expected to have sufficient funds to support<br>• David N. Keck Postdoctoral Visiting Professors,<br>• Research activities of member faculty,<br>• Student research assistants, and<br>• Other discretionary activities.<br><br>The department has a broad mission, from teaching general education classes through mentoring doctoral students and conducting research. For information about our programs and faculty, see <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/cas/math\"><strong>Mathematics Department | Ohio University</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br>Ohio University is a Carnegie Foundation R1 (doctoral universities – very high research activity) institution. It has a rich history, diverse campuses, international communities, and beautiful Appalachian settings. The city of Athens provides a classic and vibrant residential learning environment for over 20,000 students and is a family-friendly and culturally-rich community. The charm of tree-lined brick walkways on the University’s College Green makes you feel as if you are at a small college rather than a large university. Recently, Athens was rated the Best College Small Town by the readers of USA Today.</div> Mathematics <div>Salary is commensurate with experience and credentials and is accompanied by our generous university benefits such as tuition for self and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan including company contributions, parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional Information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/</strong></a>.</div> 09/03/2026 <div>12/01/2026</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/55998 2026-02-05T12:50:21-05:00 2026-02-05T12:50:22-05:00 Instructor Teacher Education Pool Posting AY 2026-2027, Curriculum and Instruction <div>The Gladys W. and David H. Patton College of Education prepares graduates who are CALLED to LEAD: Change Agents who are Lifelong Learners committed to Embracing Diversity and LEADership. Our leader-educators, practitioners, and human service professionals share our commitment to serving society responsibly as change agents in meeting diverse human and social needs.</div><ul><li>The number of Teacher Education courses offered each semester is dependent on student demand. The need may include both graduate and undergraduate courses in Curriculum and Instruction.</li><li>The successful applicant will bring strong qualifications both academically and professionally.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses on campus and/or online</li><li>Contribute to the instructional mission of the Teacher Education</li><li>Department and Patton College of Education</li><li>Using Canvas for academic engagement</li></ul> Teacher Education 02/05/2026 <div>Please apply by January 30, 2027 for full consideration.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57469 2026-08-17T11:25:35-04:00 2026-08-17T11:25:36-04:00 Athletic Trainer (up to 2 positions) Health Sciences Professions, Dean's Office https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56305 2026-03-16T21:24:59-04:00 2026-03-16T21:25:00-04:00 Instructor, University Clinical  Pool Posting <div>The Gladys W. and David H. Patton College of Education at Ohio University invites</div><div>applicants for the Adjunct Instructor position to serve as University Clinical Educators. This</div><div>position requires on-site presence in Athens, OH.<br><br></div><div>The Instructor serving as a University Clinical Educator is an integral part of The Patton</div><div>College of Education faculty and assumes responsibility for mentoring, supervising, and instructing Clinical and Professional Interns. The UCE works closely with the Coordinator of Professional Internships in Teaching and is expected to keep the PI Coordinator fully informed of the day-to-day operation of the internships and the progress of the interns assigned to them. The UCE must become familiar with the placement schools and their communities.</div> Teacher Education 03/16/2026 <div>Please apply by March 1, 2027.&nbsp;</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57576 2026-08-28T11:39:46-04:00 2026-08-28T11:39:46-04:00 Student Admissions Assistant <div>Undergraduate Admissions at Zanesville Campus&nbsp;</div> Admissions <div>$11.50</div> 08/28/2026 12/01/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57293 2026-07-28T13:31:39-04:00 2026-07-28T13:31:40-04:00 Student IT Support Specialist (SOUTHERN CAMPUS) <div>The Ohio University<strong> Southern Campus</strong> invites applications for the position of Student IT Support Specialist. This position will work on the Southern campus which is located in Ironton, Ohio. Specific departmental duties may include:<br><br></div><div><strong>Help Desk Support</strong></div><div>· Answering the help desk phone, entering work orders, and resolving issues when possible</div><div>· Check out and deliver equipment</div><div>· Assisting with inventory, testing, and cleaning of computer equipment.</div><div>· Supporting campus projects as needed<br><br></div><div><strong>OULN Classroom Operator Support</strong><br>· Responsible to be sure equipment is powered, connected and functioning for class</div><div>· Distribute and collect papers, assignments, etc. before class and returning to the proper department/location immediately after class</div><div>· Log any classroom technical issues and relay information to appropriate support team using the Teams application<br><br></div><div><strong>Campus Event Support</strong></div><div>· Setup computer, audio and AV equipment for scheduled campus events</div><div>· Operate equipment during event</div><div>· Troubleshoot any issues and resolve as necessary</div><div>· Return equipment to appropriate storage location(s) when event ends<br><br></div> Regional Higher Education <div>$11.00 per hour</div> 07/28/2026 11/30/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56723 2026-05-18T10:36:27-04:00 2026-05-18T10:36:28-04:00 Instructor (part-time) College of Business Finance Academic year 2026-2027 (POOL) <div>We are accepting resumes for potential openings in the College of Business Finance department for summer 2026 and the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.<br><br>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track instructor positions for courses offered by the College of Business on the Athens campus as departmental/student demand dictates.<br><br>The number of courses offered each semester by the College of Business is largely dependent on full-time faculty leave of absences and student demand. Therefore, we often have the need for part-time instructors with very short notice. Such part-time positions will be filled utilizing qualified applicants from this pool.<br><br>When applying, applicants should specify qualifications / interest for specific disciplines and courses. Course descriptions for undergraduate courses can be found online at <a href=\"https://catalogs.ohio.edu/\"><strong>https://catalogs.ohio.edu/</strong></a>.<br><br>Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis.<br><br><strong>Our Mission at the College of Business</strong><br>We inspire innovators who strategically create value and motivate leaders who serve with grit and determination. We also nurture self-aware citizens who better the world of business.<br><br><strong>About Ohio University</strong><br>Ohio University strives to be the best student-centered, transformative learning community in America, where approximately 30,000 students realize their promise, faculty advance knowledge, staff achieve excellence, and alumni become global leaders. Our Athens Campus offers students a vibrant residential learning experience in one of the nation’s most picturesque academic settings. Additional campuses and centers serve students across the state, and online programs further advance the University’s commitment to providing educational access and opportunity.</div> Finance, College of Business 05/18/2026 <div>4/14/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57633 2026-09-04T16:20:35-04:00 2026-09-04T16:20:36-04:00 Associate/Senior Associate Athletic Director for Business and Administrative Operations ICA Business Administration https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56068 2026-02-16T15:22:01-05:00 2026-02-16T15:22:02-05:00 School of Dance On-Campus Instructors (POOL POSTING) <div>This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Summer 2026 and Academic Year 2026-27 in Dance.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Dance to teach on-campus courses as needed.</div> School of Dance 02/16/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57500 2026-08-19T12:09:41-04:00 2026-08-19T12:09:41-04:00 Kids on Campus Afterschool Teacher (Pool Posting) Kids On Campus https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56307 2026-03-16T21:31:24-04:00 2026-03-16T21:31:25-04:00 Teacher Education Instructor, Reading Education, part-time [Pool Posting] <div>The Gladys W. and David H. Patton College of Education prepares graduates who are CALLED to LEAD: Change Agents who are Lifelong Learners committed to Embracing Diversity and LEADership. Our leader-educators, practitioners, and human service professionals share our commitment to serving society responsibly as change agents in meeting diverse human and social needs.<br><br>The number of Teacher Education courses offered each semester is dependent on student demand. The need may include both graduate and undergraduate courses in Reading Education. The successful applicant will bring strong qualifications both academically and professionally.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses on campus and/or online.</li><li>Contribute to the instructional mission of the Teacher Education</li><li>Department and Patton College of Education.</li><li>Using Canvas for academic engagement</li></ul> Teacher Education 03/16/2026 <div>Please apply by 03/02/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57590 2026-09-01T14:56:26-04:00 2026-09-01T14:56:27-04:00 Staff Counselor Counseling and Psych Services https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57295 2026-07-28T13:45:35-04:00 2026-07-28T13:45:36-04:00 Student IT Support Specialist (ZANESVILLE CAMPUS) <div>The Ohio University <strong>Zanesville Campus</strong> invites applications for the position of Student IT Support Specialist. This position will work on the Zanesville campus which is located in Zanesville, Ohio. Specific departmental duties may include:<br><br></div><div><strong>Help Desk Support</strong></div><div>· Answering the help desk phone, entering work orders, and resolving issues when possible</div><div>· Check out and deliver equipment</div><div>· Assisting with inventory, testing, and cleaning of computer equipment.</div><div>· Supporting campus projects as needed<br><br></div><div><strong>OULN Classroom Operator Support</strong><br> · Responsible to be sure equipment is powered, connected and functioning for class</div><div>· Distribute and collect papers, assignments, etc. before class and return to the proper department/location immediately after class</div><div>· Log any classroom technical issues and relay information to appropriate support team using the Teams application<br><br></div><div><strong>Campus Event Support</strong></div><div>· Setup computer, audio and AV equipment for scheduled campus events</div><div>· Operate equipment during event</div><div>· Troubleshoot any issues and resolve as necessary</div><div>· Return equipment to appropriate storage location(s) when event ends</div> Regional Higher Education <div>$11.00 per hour</div> 07/28/2026 11/30/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56780 2026-05-22T16:31:54-04:00 2026-05-22T16:31:55-04:00 School of Nursing Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Chillicothe Campus, Beginning Fall Semester 2026 (POOL POSTING) <div>The Ohio University School of Nursing, Chillicothe Campus, seeks adjunct clinical focus faculty candidates with an emphasis on teaching clinical competencies to Associate and Bachelor Degree Nursing students. These positions are term positions and will be filled as need arises for the Chillicothe campus.<br><br>Faculty are expected to plan, implement, and evaluate instruction for student clinical and simulation lab experiences. These individuals will provide instruction, supervision, guidance, and counsel to nursing students in relation to BSN program objectives and will include (1) planning student learning experiences; (2) evaluating student progress; (3) recording and reporting as required by the School of Nursing.<br><br>Clinical sites are located in the following areas of Ohio:<br>Circleville, OH<br>Chillicothe, OH<br>Columbus, OH<br>Gallipolis, OH<br>Greenfield, OH<br>Jackson, OH<br>Lucasville, OH<br>Portsmouth, OH<br><br>Seeking experience in:<br>Obstetrics<br>Pediatrics<br>Mental Health<br>Medical Surgery<br>Gerontology<br><br>The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.</div> CHILI Nursing <div>Hourly rate based on level of education.</div> 05/22/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until September 15, 2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56070 2026-02-16T15:22:32-05:00 2026-02-16T15:22:33-05:00 School of Film On-Campus Instructors (POOL POSTING) <div>This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Summer 2026 and Academic Year 2026-27 in Film.<br><br>This posting is for teaching in-person synchronous courses at the Athens campus. Course topics will vary based on need, but may include Film Studies, Screenwriting, or Film Production.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Film.</div> School of Film 02/16/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57515 2026-08-20T15:46:44-04:00 2026-08-20T15:46:44-04:00 School of Nursing Graduate Level Program Fixed-Term Instructor Academic Year 2026-2027 (Pool) <div>Ohio University School of Nursing is seeking applications for individuals to serve in adjunct (part-time) positions for the 2026-2027 academic year in various capacities as need arises in our graduate-level MSN and DNP programs and tracks. This includes, but is not limited to, lecturers, clinical supervisors, clinical instructors, lab instructors, and teaching assistants. These individuals will provide instruction, supervision, guidance and counsel to graduate-level nursing students in relation to program objectives and includes (1) planning learning experiences; (2) evaluating learners’ progress; (3) recording and reporting as required by the School of Nursing programs.<br><br>The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.</div> Nursing-Athens <div><br>Hourly rate is commensurate with highest nursing degree.</div> 04/27/2026 <div>05/31/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57297 2026-07-28T13:49:06-04:00 2026-07-28T13:49:07-04:00 Student IT Support Specialist (LANCASTER CAMPUS) <div>The Ohio University <strong>Lancaster Campus</strong> invites applications for the position of Student IT Support Specialist. This position will work on the Lancaster campus which is located in Lancaster, Ohio. Specific departmental duties may include:<br><br><strong>Help Desk Support</strong></div><div>· Answering the help desk phone, entering work orders, and resolving issues when possible</div><div>· Check out and deliver equipment</div><div>· Assisting with inventory, testing, and cleaning of computer equipment.</div><div>· Supporting campus projects as needed<br><br><br></div><div><strong>OULN Classroom Operator Support</strong><br> · Responsible to be sure equipment is powered, connected and functioning for class</div><div>· Distribute and collect papers, assignments, etc. before class and return to the proper department/location immediately after class</div><div>· Log any classroom technical issues and relay information to appropriate support team using the Teams application<br><br><br></div><div><strong>Campus Event Support</strong></div><div>· Setup computer, audio and AV equipment for scheduled campus events</div><div>· Operate equipment during event</div><div>· Troubleshoot any issues and resolve as necessary</div><div>· Return equipment to appropriate storage location(s) when event ends</div> Regional Higher Education <div>$11.00 per hour</div> 07/28/2026 11/30/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56415 2026-04-01T00:09:26-04:00 2026-04-01T00:09:27-04:00 Open Rank Tenure Track Cognitive Psychology Faculty (Quantitative Focus) <div>Ohio University is making a significant, university-wide investment in Brain Health and Cognition Across the Lifespan. This initiative brings together faculty expertise across the College of Health Sciences and Professions, the College of Arts and Sciences, and the Patton College of Education to advance discovery in brain health, cognition, communication, movement, and learning. Faculty hired into this cohort will join a collaborative, interdisciplinary network dedicated to understanding and enhancing cognitive and functional health across the lifespan, from early development through older adulthood. Together, these new faculty will strengthen Ohio University’s growing reputation in brain health research and education, fostering connections across disciplines and colleges. This investment reflects the University’s commitment to addressing the complex biological, behavioral, and social factors that shape brain health and to translating discoveries into meaningful outcomes that improve everyday life.</div><div><br>As part of this initiative, the Department of Psychology invites applicants for a <strong>tenure-track (open rank) faculty position in Cognitive Psychology</strong>. This position will begin on August 16, 2027, with the possibility of an earlier start date of January 1, 2027. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a programmatic research agenda with strong potential for extramural funding, expertise in cognitive psychology, and advanced quantitative skills. Preference will be given to applicants whose research program <strong>complements ongoing initiatives in healthy aging,</strong> including for example, the application of quantitative methods and/or computational modeling to advance understanding of how cognitive functions change with age or are impacted by injury or disease.</div><div><br>Ohio University is a Carnegie Foundation R1 (highest research activity) institution, and the successful applicant will demonstrate a strong research record. Reflecting the department’s commitment to collaborative, cross-disciplinary scholarship, research specialties often cut across both the experimental and clinical psychology programs. Pertinent to this search, many current faculty have concentrated expertise in aging, stress, and health, and welcome new partnerships. Multiple resources for developing and maintaining a strong research program are available, including infrastructure for grant procurement, grant mentoring, research lab space, start-up funds, and support for graduate students (stipends, tuition waivers, research and travel support). Of note, faculty hired into this cohort will have additional support for graduate students as research assistants.</div><div><br>Responsibilities include maintaining an active, high-quality, fundable research program, directing graduate student research, teaching graduate and undergraduate courses, and participating in departmental service. The teaching load is typically 1-2 courses each semester during the 9-month academic calendar.</div><div><br>Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community.&nbsp; Athens, home of Ohio University, provides a classic and vibrant residential learning environment for over 30,000 students, and is a family-friendly and culturally rich community. The charm of treelined brick walkways on the University’s College Green makes you feel as if you are at a small college rather than a large university. Athens is frequently cited as one of the best college towns in America, including by USA Today and World Atlas.</div><div><br>The Department of Psychology is home to 33 full-time faculty who serve over 1,400 undergraduate students and 60 graduate students across the main and seven regional campuses in Southern and Central Ohio. Committed to excellence in research, teaching, and service, the department is consistently recognized as one of the top departments at Ohio University for its outstanding research and student engagement. The psychology program is within the College of Arts &amp; Sciences and is central to Ohio University’s transformative learning experience.</div> Psychology <div>Salary is commensurate with experience and credentials and is accompanied by our generous university benefits such as tuition for self and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan including company contributions, parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional Information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/</strong></a>.</div> 04/01/2026 <div>09/15/2026</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57594 2026-09-02T08:32:49-04:00 2026-09-02T08:32:50-04:00 Project Coordinator - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine HCOM - Social Medicine https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56794 2026-05-27T09:52:30-04:00 2026-05-27T09:52:31-04:00 Arts Administration On-Campus Instructors (POOL POSTING) <div>This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Academic Year 2026-27 in Arts Administration.<br><br>This posting is for teaching in-person synchronous courses at the Athens campus. Course topics will vary based on need, but may include “Intro to Arts Administration”, “Funding and Development for Arts Organizations”, and “Concepts, Communications, Considerations in Arts Management”<br><br></div> Art 05/27/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by May 27, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56072 2026-02-16T15:23:06-05:00 2026-02-16T15:23:07-05:00 Interior Architecture Instructor - Asynchronous Online Program, School of Art + Design (Pool Posting) <div>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions for delivering asynchronous online courses in our Interior Architecture - Online Program during the 2026/2027 academic year.<br><br></div> Art 02/16/2026 <div>Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57525 2026-08-21T13:27:49-04:00 2026-08-21T13:27:50-04:00 Records Management Specialist <div>Oversees file storage and records management. Organizes, converts, and integrates files for storage. Locates and retrieves records as requested.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>Job Responsibilities&nbsp;<br>• Provides customer service to students, staff, faculty, parents, and others in the University community by solving problems regarding records and/or data.&nbsp;<br>• May lead and/or supervise TAS staff and/or student employees.&nbsp;<br>• Coordinates, and maintains a complex record system or database of specialized records.&nbsp;<br>• Researches complex record or data problems and provides recommendations or resolution. Makes decisions by reviewing information against guidelines such as transfer credit evaluation.&nbsp;<br>• Coordinates the processing, maintaining, and monitoring of records and/or data. Audits record activity to ensure compliance and accuracy.&nbsp;<br>• Serves as primary contact for release and protection of confidential and sensitive records.&nbsp;<br>• Implements and oversees guidelines for deletion of records.&nbsp;<br>• Prepares, analyzes, and distributes reports.&nbsp;<br>• Maintains awareness of governmental regulations and interprets policies, procedures and guidelines.&nbsp;<br><br></div> Registrar's Office <div>Starting pay range $16.84 – $21.48<br><br>Ohio University is proud to offer a robust healthcare plan that includes maternity care, transgender care, counseling and mental healthcare, prescription coverage, vision, dental, orthodontia care, and more. Our robust benefits package also includes paid holidays, sick time, personal time, an instructional fee waiver up to 100% for self and dependents, an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% employer contribution, a 12-week parental leave program, adoption reimbursement, flextime and flexplace policies, an employee assistance program, access to professional development programs, wellbeing incentive programs, and additional employee resources. Additional information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits</strong></a></div> 08/21/2026 <div>09/07/2026</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/53257 2025-04-25T19:12:42-04:00 2025-04-25T19:12:43-04:00 School of Nursing Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Eastern Campus, Beginning Academic Year 2025-2026 (POOL POSTING) <div>The Ohio University School of Nursing Eastern Campus seeks adjunct clinical focus faculty candidates with an emphasis on teaching clinical competencies with bachelor’s degree nursing students. These positions are term positions and will be filled as needs arise for the Eastern campus. Faculty are expected to plan, implement, and evaluate instruction for student clinical and simulation lab experiences. These individuals will provide instruction, supervision, guidance and counsel to nursing students in relation to BSN program objectives and includes (1) planning student learning experiences; (2) evaluating student progress; (3) recording and reporting as required by the School of Nursing.<br><br>Clinical sites are located in the following areas:<br>Barnesville, OH<br>Bellaire, OH<br>Belmont, OH<br>Cambridge, OH<br>Martins Ferry, OH<br>Shadyside, OH<br>Steubenville, OH<br>St. Clairsville, OH<br>Glen Dale, WV<br>Wheeling, WV<br><br>Seeking experience in:<br>Obstetrics<br>Pediatrics<br>Mental Health<br>Medical Surgical<br><br>The need for these positions is undetermined currently and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.</div> ESTRN Nursing <div>Compensation is an hourly rate commensurate on highest achieved nursing degree.</div> 04/24/2025 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until May 31, 2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57325 2026-07-30T14:40:41-04:00 2026-07-30T14:40:42-04:00 Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Tenure Track) Diabetes Mellitus and Cardiometabolic Disorders, Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine, Athens Campus (3 positions available) <div>The Diabetes Institute (DI) within the Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine (HCOM) at Ohio University is undergoing a targeted expansion to complement and strengthen its research portfolio. As part of this growth, DI/HCOM is seeking applications for three research-intensive, full-time (academic year) tenured or tenure-track faculty members at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. We welcome applications from individuals as well as teams with complementary skills and expertise, including scientists at all career stages—from early career to senior investigators.<br><br>Endowment opportunities may be awarded to exceptional candidates with an established record of clinical and translational research excellence.<br><br>Faculty in these positions will be provided substantial <strong><em>protected research time</em></strong> (negotiable for up to 80% FTE), competitive startup packages and access to Ohio University’s expanding research infrastructure.<br><br></div><div>Selected candidates will join a group of active, extramurally funded investigators within the Ohio University Diabetes Institute (<a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/di\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/di</strong></a>) whose research focuses on metabolism, nutrition and cardiometabolic diseases, including obesity, diabetes, cardiovascular disease, and associated metabolic disorders. DI faculty collaborate extensively with other HCOM faculty members with research and teaching expertise in musculoskeletal diseases, brain health, cancer, aging, epidemiology, and social determinants of health. The mission of the DI extends beyond research and is to improve the quality of life for those affected by diabetes and related diseases through not only innovative basic and applied research, but also progressive patient care, education, and community outreach.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>About the Ohio University Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine</strong></div><div><br><strong>Mission</strong><br> We pride ourselves on our strong focus on our mission: training osteopathic primary care physicians to serve Ohio. Our medical school educates physicians committed to practice in Ohio, emphasizes primary care, engages in focused research, and embraces both Appalachian and urban communities. Integral to this mission, our college community commits itself to: provide a clinically integrated, learning-centered, osteopathic medical education continuum for students, interns, residents and primary care associates; embrace public service; and improve the health and well-being of underserved populations.</div><div><br><strong>Vision</strong><br> The Heritage College is recognized as the national leader in training osteopathic primary care physicians and the number one producer of primary care physicians in the country.</div><div><br><strong>Essential Values</strong><br> These fundamental principles form the foundation of the culture at our college: wholeness and balance within each person; integrity; community of mutual respect; acceptance of others; pursuit of excellence; a climate of scholarship; and commitment to service, generosity and compassion.</div><div><br><strong>Our Campuses:</strong><br><a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses</strong></a><br> <br> <strong>HCOM Admissions:</strong><br> <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-admissions\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-admissions</strong></a></div> HCOM - Diabetes Institute <div>Salary is commensurate with rank, experience and credentials. Salary is accompanied by our generous university benefits such as tuition for self and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% company contribution, parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional Information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/</strong></a>.</div> 07/30/2026 <div>9/20/2026</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56446 2026-04-06T09:34:55-04:00 2026-04-06T09:34:56-04:00 Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine, Athens Campus (Pool Posting) <div><strong>Position Description:</strong></div><div>The Ohio University Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine (OU-HCOM) is seeking an Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) physician for a part-time (16 hours per week) faculty teaching position at the Athens, Ohio campus.<br><br>Applicants should possess a strong desire to teach and advise osteopathic medical students within the curriculum and contribute to the success of the Heritage College and its campuses through teaching and service. Candidates must have outstanding interpersonal skills to relate to a diverse faculty, staff, students and community members.<br><br>The successful applicant will have special interest and qualifications in the practice and teaching of osteopathic principles and manipulative medicine.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Prepare and deliver curricular and other scholarly activities.</li><li>Teach the clinical application of osteopathic principles and manipulative medicine in ambulatory and hospital-based practices.</li><li>Participate in the ongoing programs and program development of the Department of OMM including pre- and postdoctoral training and other scholarly activities as appropriate.</li></ul><div><br><strong>About the Ohio University Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine</strong></div><div><br><strong>Mission</strong><br> We pride ourselves on our strong focus on our mission: training osteopathic primary care physicians to serve Ohio. Our medical school educates physicians committed to practice in Ohio, emphasizes primary care, engages in focused research, and embraces both Appalachian and urban communities. Integral to this mission, our college community commits itself to: provide a clinically integrated, learning-centered, osteopathic medical education continuum for students, interns, residents and primary care associates; embrace diversity and public service; and improve the health and well-being of underserved populations.</div><div><br><strong>Vision</strong><br> The Heritage College is recognized as the national leader in training osteopathic primary care physicians and the number one producer of primary care physicians in the country.</div><div><br><strong>Essential Values</strong><br> These fundamental principles form the foundation of the culture at our college: wholeness and balance within each person; integrity; community of mutual respect; acceptance of others and embracing diversity; pursuit of excellence; a climate of scholarship; and commitment to service, generosity and compassion.</div><div><br><strong>Our Campuses:</strong><br> <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/about/campuses</strong></a><br> <br> <strong>HCOM Admissions:</strong><br> <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-admissions\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-admissions</strong></a></div> HCOM - Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) <div>Salary will be commensurate with education and experience, while also considering internal equity. Incumbent will also enjoy a generous benefits package including paid holidays, sick time, a pro-rated tuition waiver based on FTE for the faculty member and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% company contribution, flextime and flexplace policies, counseling and mental health care, access to professional faculty development programs and more. Additional information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits</strong></a>.</div> 04/06/2026 <div>4/5/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57597 2026-09-02T10:51:37-04:00 2026-09-02T10:51:37-04:00 Postdoctoral Researcher for Dr. Sharma - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine HCOM - Biomedical Sciences https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57528 2026-08-21T14:02:46-04:00 2026-08-21T14:02:47-04:00 Student Social Media & Digital Engagement Assistant <div>The Ohio Innovation Exchange (OIEx) is seeking a student to support the digital communications and social media presence, with a primary focus on LinkedIn. OIEx is a statewide initiative led by OHIO that connects Ohio businesses, industries, and organizations with the expertise, facilities, and resources of Ohio's colleges and universities.<br><br></div><ul><li>Create, schedule, and publish social media content, primarily on LinkedIn.</li><li>Promote OIEx success stories, partnerships, events, and opportunities.</li><li>Monitor social media activity and respond to comments, questions, and messages in a professional and timely manner.</li><li>Assist with the development of graphics, short videos, and other digital content.</li><li>Track engagement metrics and provide periodic reports on audience growth and content performance.</li><li>Identify opportunities to expand OIEx visibility and engagement across Ohio's innovation ecosystem.</li><li>Coordinate with OIEx staff and partner organizations to gather content and highlight impactful collaborations.</li></ul> VP For Research <div>This part time student position will pay $11 per hour for the academic year.</div> 08/21/2026 09/06/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56850 2026-06-03T16:23:45-04:00 2026-06-03T16:23:45-04:00 Instructor, English (Part-time, Non-tenure track) POOL POSTING <div>The English department is seeking applicants for a part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor position at the Athens campus for the Fall 2026 semester and the 2026-2027 academic year. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will review and select candidates from this posting. Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis through the close date listed in this posting.<br><br>The instructor will teach first-year and/or advanced composition or another writing or literature course as assigned.<br><br>Please see <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/cas/english\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/cas/english</strong></a> for details about the English program.<br><br><strong>English Department: </strong>The Department of English has 29 full-time faculty across the main campus and seven regional campuses and centers in Southern and Central Ohio. Situated within the College of Arts &amp; Sciences, the Department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service to the students it serves in the undergraduate major, M.A. and Ph.D. degree programs, and across the university in writing and humanities general education courses. To learn more about the successes of our English Department and student programs, visit; <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/cas/english\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/cas/english</strong></a>.<br><br><strong>College of Arts &amp; Sciences:</strong> This college is central to Ohio University’s transformative learning experience. The foundational instruction for the entire university, delivered through the general education and liberal arts curriculum, is provided by the College of Arts and Sciences. The college provides the primary instruction for approximately one-third of the undergraduate majors on campus, as well as half of the undergraduate credit hours on the Athens campus. In addition, the college offers a number of master’s programs, and eight departments offer doctoral degrees. A&amp;S faculty are at the heart of Ohio University’s research activity.</div><div><br><strong>Ohio University.</strong> Established in 1804, Ohio University is the oldest public university in the state of Ohio. Our total enrollment is over 28,000 students across the state and online. About 20,000 of those students are undergraduates studying at our residential campus in Athens—our quintessential college town that’s nestled deep in the Appalachian foothills of beautiful Southeast Ohio. Our picturesque campus is located in the foothills of the Appalachian Mountains amidst scenic state and national parks, and is just 75 minutes southeast of Columbus, Ohio.<br><br></div> English <div>Pay is set according to college approved rates. Please visit <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/cas/dean/faculty-affairs/summer-overload-guidelines\"><strong>A&amp;S Summer and Overload Course Policy | Ohio University</strong></a> for more information. Pay is accompanied by an excellent retirement plan and paid sick time.</div> 06/03/2026 <div>05/30/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56074 2026-02-16T15:24:04-05:00 2026-02-16T15:24:05-05:00 Art History Instructor - Athens Campus, School of Art + Design (POOL POSTING) <div>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions for delivering in-person courses at the Athens Campus for our Art History Department during the 2026/2027 academic year.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Art + Design.</div> Art 02/16/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 14, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/55244 2025-09-12T10:55:10-04:00 2025-09-12T10:55:11-04:00 Intermittent Mobile Health Unit Driver (POOL) - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine HCOM - Community Health Programs https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57422 2026-08-12T11:47:40-04:00 2026-08-12T11:47:40-04:00 Culinary Services - Quality Assurance Assistant (Student/Entry-Level) <ul><li>Maintain the Manufacturing log.</li><li>Check food safety and quality assurance records.</li><li>Support daily monitoring of food preparation, storage, and production areas.</li><li>Verify that sanitation and hygiene procedures are followed.</li><li>Participate in internal audits and food safety inspections.</li><li>Confidence in training students.</li><li>Support employee food safety training activities as needed.</li><li>Perform other quality assurance and food safety duties as assigned.</li></ul> Culinary Services - Central Food <div><br>PL4-14.00/hr for Assistant Work</div> 08/12/2026 09/07/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56454 2026-04-06T15:28:48-04:00 2026-04-06T15:28:49-04:00 School of Nursing Adjunct Clinical Faculty Lancaster Campus, Beginning Fall 2026 (POOL POSTING) <div>The Ohio University School of Nursing Lancaster Campus seeks adjunct clinical focus faculty candidates with an emphasis on teaching clinical competencies to bachelor’s degree nursing students. These positions are term positions and will be filled as needs arise for the Lancaster campus. Faculty are expected to plan, implement, and evaluate instruction for student clinical and simulation lab experiences. These individuals will provide instruction, supervision, guidance and counsel to nursing students in relation to BSN program objectives and includes (1) planning student learning experiences; (2) evaluating student progress; (3) recording and reporting as required by the School of Nursing.<br><br>Clinical sites are located in the following areas:<br>Lancaster, OH</div><div>Columbus, OH</div><div><br>Seeking experience in:<br>Medical / Surgical</div><div>Gerontology</div><div>Mental Health</div><div><br>The need for these positions is undetermined currently and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.</div> LNCSTR Nursing <div>Hourly rate per degree of education.</div> 04/06/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until September 15, 2026.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57601 2026-09-02T12:55:43-04:00 2026-09-02T12:55:43-04:00 Research Instrumentation Technician Chemistry and Biochemistry https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57545 2026-08-25T14:43:04-04:00 2026-08-25T14:43:04-04:00 Department Administrator Admissions https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56996 2026-06-23T16:19:33-04:00 2026-06-23T16:19:34-04:00 POOL POSTING:  Instructor of Hearing, Speech & Language Sciences (non-tenure track) <div>We are accepting application for potential openings in the Department of Hearing, Speech and Language Sciences for fall, spring, and summer semesters of AY 2026-2027. Applications to this pool will be considered to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions at the Athens campus.<br><br>The teaching workload will vary based on departmental teaching needs each semester. Anticipated<br>needs are for the following undergraduate level courses: Introduction to Communication Disorders, Phonetics, Speech Science, and Research Methods. Graduate courses are TBD. A description of all undergraduate HSLS courses can be viewed at: <a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/3czed3zb\"><strong>https://tinyurl.com/3czed3zb</strong></a>. A description of graduate level HSLS courses can be viewed at: <a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/3kxsr57w\"><strong>https://tinyurl.com/3kxsr57w</strong></a>.</div> Hearing, Speech and Language Sciences 06/23/2026 <div>07/03/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56098 2026-02-18T13:22:05-05:00 2026-02-18T13:22:06-05:00 Foundation Program Instructor - Athens Campus, School of Art + Design  (POOL POSTING) <div>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions for delivering in-person courses at the Athens Campus for our Studio Art Foundations Program during the 2026/2027 academic year.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Art + Design.</div> Art 02/18/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/55665 2025-11-14T15:05:44-05:00 2025-11-14T15:05:44-05:00 Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor, Endocrinology or Diabetology, (Non Tenure Track) Part-Time, Athens Campus <div>We are seeking an emerging or established clinical researcher with a focus on diabetes. This applicant will join a group of active, extramurally funded investigators within the <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/di\"><strong>Ohio University Diabetes Institute</strong></a>. This role is ideal for a physician interested in joining a team to gain experience in clinical research to contribute to the success of research programs that focus on the following topics: cardiometabolic health, diabetes, obesity, cardiovascular disease and/or associated metabolic diseases. This role will also contribute to the Heritage College <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/medicine/med-education/osteopathic-medicine\"><strong>Pathways to Health and Wellness</strong></a> Curriculum and Diabetes Institute educational programming.</div><div>The mission of the DI is to improve the quality of life for those affected by diabetes and related diseases through innovative basic and applied research, progressive patient care, education, and community outreach. DI-affiliated faculty members have research and teaching expertise in diabetes, cardiovascular, musculoskeletal, cancer, aging, epidemiology, and social determinants of health.</div> HCOM - Specialty Medicine <div>Salary will be commensurate with education and experience, while also considering internal equity. Incumbent will also enjoy a generous benefits package including paid holidays, sick time, a pro-rated tuition waiver based on FTE for the faculty member and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% company contribution, a 12-week parental leave program, adoption reimbursement, flextime and flexplace policies, counseling and mental health care, access to professional development programs and more. Additional information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits</strong></a>.</div> 11/14/2025 <div>6/30/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57426 2026-08-12T13:03:06-04:00 2026-08-12T13:03:06-04:00 Student Office Assistant <div>The OHIO Chillicothe Student Services department seeks enthusiastic and engaging students to join our teams.&nbsp; Student Services Student Assistants provide support to the Student Services Department, Admissions, Shoemaker Center, and other administrative units by serving at the Bennett Hall Information Desk, Student Services Suite, and other areas of campus.&nbsp; Duties may include the following:</div><div>&nbsp;</div><ol><li>Learning and understanding campus details including units, employees, and processes in order to assist all members of the campus community.</li><li>Greeting and directing campus visitors to the appropriate campus units.</li><li>Answering and directing phone calls and resolving issues when possible.</li><li>Processing packages accurately.</li><li>Communicating with a variety of individuals and groups via speech, email, and text.</li><li>Assisting with campus activities and events as needed.</li><li>Monitoring the Shoemaker Center, assuring that all guests are properly checked-in.</li><li>Giving campus tours and other Admissions related activities.</li><li>Performing administrative tasks such as scanning, filing, organizing, and data processing.</li><li>Supporting campus projects as needed.</li><li>Other duties as assigned</li></ol><div>&nbsp;</div> CHILI Student Services-Advising <div>$11.00 PER HR</div> 08/10/2026 11/30/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56680 2026-05-11T14:31:35-04:00 2026-05-11T14:31:35-04:00 Pool posting - Instructor, Coaching, Health and Physical Education (non-tenure track) <div>Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis through 05/11/2027.Applications to this position will be utilized to fill a part-time, non-benefits eligible adjunct instructor position for online and Athens campus instruction during the 2026-2027 fall, spring and summer semesters. More specifically, the successful candidate will be responsible for teaching online and/or in-person undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the Coaching, Health &amp; Physical Education degrees, specifically in:</div><ul><li>Master of Science in Soccer Coaching Education online courses</li><li>Master of Science in Coaching Education online and/or on-campus courses</li><li>Bachelor of Science in Physical Activity &amp; Sport Coaching online and/or on-campus courses</li><li>Bachelor of Science in Physical Education &amp; Teacher Education (PETE) online and/or on-campus courses</li></ul><div><br>Adjunct instructor faculty engages students in learning that meets the course and learning objectives, and would receive instructional materials, and support for the specific course they would be hired to teach. Adjunct instructor responsibilities usually include leading class sessions, grading student work, participating in course assessment activities, and responding to student questions in a timely manner.</div> Recreation & Sport Pedagogy 05/11/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis through 05/11/2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57613 2026-09-03T10:48:18-04:00 2026-09-03T10:48:18-04:00 Part-Time Instructor, Center for Law, Justice and Culture (POOL POSTING) <div>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions as student demand dictates in the Center of Law, Justice and Culture at Ohio University.<br><br>The instructor pool may support courses designed for undergraduate students preparing for the Law School Admission Test (LSAT). Such courses build the cognitive endurance, timing, and error-analysis habits necessary to maximize competitive law school admissions scores. Courses may be offered in person or online, depending on need and demand.</div> Center for Law, Justice, and Culture <div>Pay is set according to college approved rates. Please visit <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/cas/dean/faculty-affairs/summer-overload-guidelines\"><strong>A&amp;S Summer and Overload Course Policy | Ohio University</strong></a> for more information.</div> 09/03/2026 <div>07/31/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56110 2026-02-19T10:16:03-05:00 2026-02-19T10:16:04-05:00 Intermittent/PRN Float Nurse (Pool Posting) - Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine HCOM - Community Health Programs https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57553 2026-08-27T11:48:26-04:00 2026-08-27T11:48:27-04:00 Building Automation Systems Technician 2 <div>Under general direction of a lead worker or supervision by departmental administrator performs highly skilled installation, repair, &amp; preventive maintenance on Building Automation System Controls; periodically inspects operation of equipment. Provides work direction, training and mentoring of lower-level air quality technicians and/or other trades workers performing craft duties.<br><br></div><ul><li>Adheres to all OSHA and/or Ohio University required safety guidelines.</li><li>Provides work direction, training &amp; mentoring of lower-level air quality technicians and/or trade workers performing craft duties.</li><li>Repairs air conditioning, refrigeration &amp; heating systems, thermostats, relays, valves, controls, compressors &amp; filters; solders piping as necessary.</li><li>Periodically inspects &amp; tests installed equipment for proper assembly of components, checking for any needed repairs &amp; compliance with technical orders, blueprints, schematics, diagrams, specifications, handbooks, laptops (with the appropriated software), &amp; established procedures; troubleshoots system to solve problems.</li><li>Installs &amp; operates refrigeration, air conditioning &amp; heating units.</li><li>Installs, repairs, calibrates &amp; troubleshoots pneumatic, electric, electronic, &amp; DDC controls; verifies proper installation &amp; operation using diagrams &amp; schematics; generates new documentation, suggests &amp; makes required modifications to systems as needed.</li><li>Performs inventory control, work scheduling &amp; completes necessary documentation. Uses computerized maintenance management system (CMMS).</li><li>Repairs, maintains and installs air compressors.</li><li>Performs other related duties as required.</li></ul> Controls & Instrumentation <div>AFSCME|08|$24.62 – $27.72 hourly rate</div> 08/27/2026 <div>September 10, 2026</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57088 2026-07-06T13:39:19-04:00 2026-07-06T13:39:19-04:00 Peer Tutor/Peer-Assisted Learning Leader/Undergraduate Writing Commons Tutor <div>Academic Achievement Center Peer Tutors, Peer-Assisted Learning (PAL) Leaders, and Undergraduate Writing Commons Tutors provide learning support to undergraduate students in one-hour sessions.<br><br>Peer Tutors meet with students in online Teams meetings and in-person at various locations on the Athens and regional campuses. Tutors engage students in learning activities such as discussing class material and test questions, offering information about learning strategies, and fostering a positive learning environment.<br><br>PAL Leaders facilitate weekly review sessions for students taking historically difficult courses. During PAL sessions, PAL Leaders facilitate discussion of important course concepts, help students develop strategies for studying, and teach participants how to become independent learners. In addition to facilitating weekly review sessions, PAL Leader responsibilities include attending class, communicating with the professor, and planning review sessions.<br><br>Writing Tutors also work collaboratively with students throughout the writing process by discussing academic or non-academic writing projects, developing ideas, organizing and revising drafts, and strengthening clarity and organization. Rather than editing or proofreading papers, Writing Tutors help students develop effective writing strategies, become more confident writers, and build the skills needed to write independently.<br><br>Responsibilities: Complete the required 10 hours of paid training. Attend all scheduled tutoring or PAL sessions. Be punctual, begin all sessions promptly, use time for academic tasks, and focus on the student’s needs. Create a positive learning environment and encourage independent learning by helping students identify problem areas and giving them opportunities to practice and build knowledge. Maintain confidentiality as outlined in the FERPA compliance statement. Keep up-to-date with appointments using the TracCloud scheduling software. Check email and Teams to remain informed of activity at the AAC. Submit accurate time sheets and enter hours in Workforce in a timely manner.</div> Academic Achievement Center <div>$11.30/hour</div> 07/06/2026 06/30/2027 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57622 2026-09-04T08:47:24-04:00 2026-09-04T08:47:24-04:00 Success Advisor - College of Business (Term) (Up to 2 positions) Business Career & Student Success Center https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/55735 2025-12-02T19:10:08-05:00 2025-12-02T19:10:09-05:00 POOL Posting – Instructor, Counseling and Higher Education (Non-Tenure Track) <div>Instructors selected from this pool will teach courses within the Department of Counseling and Higher Education. Courses may include foundations of counseling, group counseling, ethics, assessment, multicultural counseling, career counseling, practicum or internship supervision, and other program-specific offerings depending on departmental needs. Courses may be online, in-person, or hybrid.</div> Counseling and Higher Education <div>to be determined upon enrollment, courses taught</div> 12/02/2025 <div>Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis to fill potential vacancies as they occur. Please apply by November 30, 2026.&nbsp;</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57456 2026-08-14T17:05:32-04:00 2026-08-14T17:05:32-04:00 Administrative Specialist <div>Supports the general administrative functions of a wide variety of academic or administrative units including answering phones, greeting/referring/assisting visitors, customers, staff, or others, preparing documents and reports, compiling records, scheduling meetings, organizing and maintaining information, coordinating calendars, analyzing data including budgetary expenditures, and providing high level administrative assistance to executives.<br><br>Job Responsibilities<br>• May supervise or oversee the work of Technical &amp; Administrative Support staff and/or student employees.<br>• Resolves complex and unique problems that require an ability to interpret established policies and procedures.<br>• Oversees department unit administrative processes.<br>• Coordinates complex processes and initiatives such as grant proposals, contracts /or complex academic processes such as tenure case approvals, faculty searches, complicated course scheduling or sensitive graduate application processes.<br>• Plans and implements projects, special events, and/or programs that require a high level of coordination with multiple constituents and departments.<br>• Composes and edits internal and external correspondence and documents, including such things as manuscript submissions for scientific journals.<br>• Manages academic courses and textbook information. Plans and maintains website as well as other department publications.<br>• Prepares and monitors internal budget and other financial documents for a departmental work unit. Recommends purchases. Reviews and follows up on discrepancies in standard expenditures.</div> University Advancement <div>Target hiring range for this role is $16.84 per hour to $21.48 per hour and the final offer will be commensurate with the candidate’s education and experience in relation to the minimum qualifications for the position.</div> 08/14/2026 <div>09/13/2026</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56716 2026-05-18T10:11:25-04:00 2026-05-18T10:11:25-04:00 Instructor (part-time) College of Business Accountancy Academic year 2026-2027 (POOL) <div>We are accepting resumes for potential openings in the College of Business School of Accountancy for the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.<br><br>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track instructor positions for courses offered by the College of Business on the Athens campus as departmental/student demand dictates.<br><br>The number of courses offered each semester by the College of Business is largely dependent on full-time faculty leave of absences and student demand. Therefore, we often have the need for part-time instructors with very short notice. Such part-time positions will be filled utilizing qualified applicants from this pool.<br><br>When applying, applicants should specify qualifications / interest for specific disciplines and courses. Course descriptions for undergraduate courses can be found online at <a href=\"https://catalogs.ohio.edu/\"><strong>https://catalogs.ohio.edu/</strong></a>.<br><br>Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis.<br><br><strong>Our Mission at the College of Business</strong><br>We inspire innovators who strategically create value and motivate leaders who serve with grit and determination. We also nurture self-aware citizens who better the world of business.<br><br><strong>About Ohio University</strong><br>Ohio University strives to be the best student-centered, transformative learning community in America, where approximately 30,000 students realize their promise, faculty advance knowledge, staff achieve excellence, and alumni become global leaders. Our Athens Campus offers students a vibrant residential learning experience in one of the nation’s most picturesque academic settings. Additional campuses and centers serve students across the state, and online programs further advance the University’s commitment to providing educational access and opportunity.</div> School Of Accountancy 05/18/2026 <div>4/14/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56117 2026-02-19T14:25:06-05:00 2026-02-19T14:25:06-05:00 Interdisciplinary Arts Instructors (POOL POSTING) <div>This is a pool posting for potential adjunct needs that may arise for Summer 2026 and Academic Year 2026-27 in Interdisciplinary Arts.<br><br>We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Interdisciplinary Arts.</div> School of Interdisciplinary Arts 02/19/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57565 2026-08-27T14:33:38-04:00 2026-08-27T14:33:39-04:00 Events Manager Transportation & Parking https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57211 2026-07-16T11:35:26-04:00 2026-07-16T11:35:27-04:00 Instructor, Geography (non-tenure track, part-time) POOL POSTING <div>Applications for the positions will be considered to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions for the Department of Geography. The selected candidates may teach a large introduction level class or combined undergraduate and graduate courses. Duties include student assessment and may include teaching a lab.</div> Geography <div>Pay is set according to college approved rates. Please visit <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/cas/dean/faculty-affairs/summer-overload-guidelines\"><strong>A&amp;S Summer and Overload Course Policy | Ohio University</strong></a> for more information.</div> 07/16/2026 <div>07/15/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56718 2026-05-18T10:19:03-04:00 2026-05-18T10:19:04-04:00 Instructor (part-time) College of Business Sports Administration Academic year 2026-2027 (POOL) <div>We are accepting resumes for potential openings in the College of Business Sports Administration department for summer 2026 and the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.<br><br>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track instructor positions for courses offered by the College of Business on the Athens campus as departmental/student demand dictates.<br><br>The number of courses offered each semester by the College of Business is largely dependent on full-time faculty leave of absences and student demand. Therefore, we often have the need for part-time instructors with very short notice. Such part-time positions will be filled utilizing qualified applicants from this pool.<br><br>When applying, applicants should specify qualifications / interest for specific disciplines and courses. Course descriptions for undergraduate courses can be found online at <a href=\"https://catalogs.ohio.edu/\"><strong>https://catalogs.ohio.edu/</strong></a>.<br><br>Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis.<br><br><strong>Our Mission at the College of Business</strong><br>We inspire innovators who strategically create value and motivate leaders who serve with grit and determination. We also nurture self-aware citizens who better the world of business.<br><br><strong>About Ohio University</strong><br>Ohio University strives to be the best student-centered, transformative learning community in America, where approximately 30,000 students realize their promise, faculty advance knowledge, staff achieve excellence, and alumni become global leaders. Our Athens Campus offers students a vibrant residential learning experience in one of the nation’s most picturesque academic settings. Additional campuses and centers serve students across the state, and online programs further advance the University’s commitment to providing educational access and opportunity.</div> Sports Administration 05/18/2026 <div>4/14/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57628 2026-09-04T12:22:15-04:00 2026-09-04T12:22:16-04:00 Development Coordinator Development https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/55958 2026-01-30T16:51:11-05:00 2026-01-30T16:51:11-05:00 POOL: Data Analytics Instructor <div>University College offers several courses for students pursuing a successful completion of their degree(s). A few of the courses offered are:<br><br>1) Data Analytics courses (DATA 2100, 3510) introduce the fundamental concepts, principles, and tools of data analytics. They also teach key principles of analytic design and useful visualization techniques for the exploration and presentation of data.<br><br>2) Study Skills, Time Management, and Personal Finance courses (UC 1100, 1070, 1101) focus on the specific knowledge and skills necessary for students to be successful at the college level.<br><br>Instructors:<br>1) serve as a role model, referral, and resource to students;<br>2) provide contact information to students; communicating availability and encouraging students to contact them for assistance;<br>3) in case of an emergency or planned absence, make arrangements for a substitute instructor;<br>4) provide a complete syllabus on the first meeting of class and grade assignments in a timely manner;<br>5) submit final grades online by the university deadline; and<br>6) participate in assessment processes to determine efficacy of the courses and course materials.</div> University College, Dean's Office 01/30/2026 <div>Applications to this pool will be considered to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions as student demand dictates on the Athens campus. Position will remain open until filled.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57467 2026-08-17T10:51:09-04:00 2026-08-17T10:51:10-04:00 Senior Admissions Advisor Online, Transfer and Credit Services Center https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56194 2026-03-02T12:29:35-05:00 2026-03-02T12:29:36-05:00 Art Education Instructor- Athens Campus, School of Art + Design (POOL POSTING) <div>ART 5620 is a required course in the one-year Master of Education in Art Education program and plays a central role in preparing candidates for effective, standards-aligned K–12 art instruction. The course emphasizes standards-based curriculum development, assessment strategies, inclusive teaching practices, classroom management, and supervised clinical teaching in public schools.<br><br>Primary instructional responsibilities include developing and delivering course content aligned with Ohio standards, guiding students in lesson planning and unit development, designing assessments, modeling appropriate studio processes for K–12 classrooms, and evaluating student work while providing timely, constructive feedback.<br><br>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions for delivering of a in-person course at the Athens Campus for our Masters in Education in Art Education during the 2026/2027 academic year.</div> Art 03/02/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis. Please apply by February 16, 2027.</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57575 2026-08-28T11:08:18-04:00 2026-08-28T11:08:18-04:00 Student Admissions Assistant <div>Student Admissions Assistants \"Ambassadors\" serve as the student face of Ohio University Southern by welcoming prospective students and families, supporting recruitment initiatives, and promoting the university throughout the Tri-State region. Through conversations and peer-to-peer engagement, ambassadors help prospective students explore educational opportunities, navigate the enrollment process, and envision themselves as future Bobcats.<br><br></div><div>Student Ambassadors work collaboratively with Admissions, the Office of Student Services, faculty, and campus partners to support recruitment events, campus visits, community outreach, and student engagement activities while fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus environment.</div> Admissions <div>Hourly rate based on university student employment pay scale.</div> 08/28/2026 12/01/2026 https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57286 2026-07-27T11:33:35-04:00 2026-07-27T11:33:36-04:00 Certified Flight Instructor 2 (Pool Posting) Aviation https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56720 2026-05-18T10:26:20-04:00 2026-05-18T10:26:20-04:00 Instructor (part-time) College of Business, Marketing, Academic year 2026-2027 (POOL) <div>We are accepting resumes for potential openings in the College of Business Marketing department for summer 2026 and the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.<br><br>Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track instructor positions for courses offered by the College of Business on the Athens campus as departmental/student demand dictates.<br><br>The number of courses offered each semester by the College of Business is largely dependent on full-time faculty leave of absences and student demand. Therefore, we often have the need for part-time instructors with very short notice. Such part-time positions will be filled utilizing qualified applicants from this pool.<br><br>When applying, applicants should specify qualifications / interest for specific disciplines and courses. Course descriptions for undergraduate courses can be found online at https://catalogs.ohio.edu/.<br><br>Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis.<br><br><strong>Our Mission at the College of Business</strong><br>We inspire innovators who strategically create value and motivate leaders who serve with grit and determination. We also nurture self-aware citizens who better the world of business.<br><br><strong>About Ohio University</strong><br>Ohio University strives to be the best student-centered, transformative learning community in America, where approximately 30,000 students realize their promise, faculty advance knowledge, staff achieve excellence, and alumni become global leaders. Our Athens Campus offers students a vibrant residential learning experience in one of the nation’s most picturesque academic settings. Additional campuses and centers serve students across the state, and online programs further advance the University’s commitment to providing educational access and opportunity.<br><br></div> Marketing 05/18/2026 <div>4/14/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57630 2026-09-04T14:16:07-04:00 2026-09-04T14:16:07-04:00 Accounting Support Senior Specialist <div>Supports the organization's accounting functions. Maintains up-to-date and accurate records of daily transactions, accounts receivable, accounts payable, inventories, payroll, and various other records.<br><br>•Serves as the initial contact for customers. Mentors, coaches, and trains lower level employees on customer service and department policies.<br>•Often directs work, trains, and/or supervises other staff or student employees.<br>•Performs financial analyses and makes recommendations based on data.<br>•Reviews the work of other employees for accuracy and compliance with accepted standards and University policies.<br>•Completes and submits institutional surveys for publishers and agencies.<br>•Issues purchase orders in accordance with functional policy. Communicates with internal and external customers to manage purchasing.<br>•Analyzes and monitors department and program budgets. Approves and tracks expenditures.</div> Arts and Sciences, Dean's Office <div>The starting salary range is $16.84 per hour up to $21.48 per hour, dependent on education and prior experience and is accompanied by our generous university benefits such as tuition for self and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan including company contributions, parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional Information is available at: <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/</strong></a>.</div> 08/28/2026 <div>09/13/2026</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56023 2026-02-10T08:37:26-05:00 2026-02-10T08:37:26-05:00 Instructor, Psychology (non-tenure track, part-time) (POOL) <div>Applications to this pool will be considered to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions for the Department of Psychology.</div> Psychology <div>Pay is set according to college approved rates. Please visit <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/cas/dean/faculty-affairs/summer-overload-guidelines\"><strong>A&amp;S Summer and Overload Course Policy | Ohio University</strong></a> for more information. Pay is accompanied by an excellent retirement plan and paid sick leave.&nbsp; OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional Information is available at <a href=\"https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/\"><strong>https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/.</strong></a></div> 02/10/2026 <div>02/09/2027</div> https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57496 2026-08-18T18:18:58-04:00 2026-08-18T18:18:59-04:00 Instructor - Civil and Environmental Engineering (POOL Posting) <div>The Russ College of Engineering &amp; Technology's Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at Ohio University invites applications for part-time Instructors (non-tenure track) in Civil and Environmental Engineering. Candidates with prior experience teaching in-person or on-line courses and those who have practical experience in the focus areas are preferred.<br><br>Candidates with expertise in any of the following focus areas of Civil or Environmental Engineering should apply: construction engineering management, environmental, geotechnical, statistics, structural, surveying, or transportation.</div> Civil Engineering <div>Commensurate with credentials and experience</div> 08/14/2026 <div>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until August 12, 2027.</div>"
    },
