n courses at the Athens Campus for our undergraduate and/or graduate programs in the following studio art Areas: Ceramics, Digital Art + Technology, Painting + Drawing, Printmaking, Photography + Integrated Media, and Sculpture + Expanded Practice during the 202... View Details Bookmark Arts Administration On-Campus Instructors (POOL POSTING) 05/27/2026 05/27/2027 Art Athens, Ohio This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Academic Year 2026-27 in Arts Administration.This posting is for teaching in-person synchronous courses at the Athens campus. Course topics will vary based on need, but may include “Intro to Arts Administration”, “Funding and Development for Arts Organizations”, and “Concepts, Communications, Considerations in Arts Managem... View Details Bookmark Interior Architecture Instructor - Athens Campus, School of Art + Design (Pool Posting) 02/16/2026 02/16/2027 Art Athens, Ohio Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions for delivering in-person courses at the Athens Campus in our Interior Architecture Department during the 2026/2027 academic year. View Details Bookmark Graphic Design Instructor - Athens Campus, School of Art + Design  (POOL POSTING) 02/16/2026 02/16/2027 Art Athens, Ohio Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions for delivering in-person courses at the Athens Campus for our Graphic Design Department during the 2026/2027 academic year.We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Art + Design. View Details Bookmark Foundation Program Instructor - Asynchronous Online Program, School of Art + Design (POOL POSTING) 02/18/2026 02/16/2027 Art Athens, Ohio Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible Instructor positions delivering asynchronous online courses in our Studio Art Foundations Program during the 2026/2027 academic year.We are looking for industry professionals for potential instructional opportunities in Art + Design. View Details Bookmark Art Education Instructor- Athens Campus, School of Art + Design (POOL POSTING) 03/02/2026 02/16/2027 Art Athens, Ohio ART 5620 is a required course in the one-year Master of Education in Art Education program and plays a central role in preparing candidates for effective, standards-aligned K–12 art instruction. The course emphasizes standards-based curriculum development, assessment strategies, inclusive teaching practices, classroom management, and supervised clinical teaching in public schools.Primary instru... View Details Bookmark Instructor (part-time) College of Business Graduate & Professional Programs Academic year 2026-2027 (POOL) 05/18/2026 04/14/2027 Business Graduate & Professional Programs Athens, Ohio We are accepting resumes for potential openings in the College of Business Graduate & Professional Programs for Summer 2026 the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.Applications to this pool will be ut... View Details Bookmark Part-Time Instructor, Center for Law, Justice and Culture (POOL POSTING) 09/03/2026 07/31/2027 Center for Law, Justice, and Culture Athens, Ohio Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions as student demand dictates in the Center of Law, Justice and Culture at Ohio University.The instructor pool may support courses designed for undergraduate students preparing for the Law School Admission Test (LSAT). Such courses build the cognitive endurance, timing, and er... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Instruction, Child Development Center (Teacher) 08/22/2026 09/13/2026 Child Development Center Athens, Ohio Context: The Patton College has four Core Values: 1) Preparing ethical and reflective leader-educators and human service professionals, 2) Lifelong learning, 3) Change agency and 4) Diversity. At its core, the College is committed to serving a diverse student population that includes international and non-traditional students and to providing service to the region through professional engagemen... View Details Bookmark School of Nursing Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Chillicothe Campus, Beginning Fall Semester 2026 (POOL POSTING) 05/22/2026 09/15/2026 CHILI Nursing Chillicothe, Ohio The Ohio University School of Nursing, Chillicothe Campus, seeks adjunct clinical focus faculty candidates with an emphasis on teaching clinical competencies to Associate and Bachelor Degree Nursing students. These positions are term positions and will be filled as need arises for the Chillicothe campus.Faculty are expected to plan, implement, and evaluate instruction for student clinical and s... View Details Bookmark Instructor - Civil and Environmental Engineering (POOL Posting) 08/14/2026 08/12/2027 Civil Engineering Athens, Ohio The Russ College of Engineering & Technology’s Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at Ohio University invites applications for part-time Instructors (non-tenure track) in Civil and Environmental Engineering. Candidates with prior experience teaching in-person or on-line courses and those who have practical experience in the focus areas are preferred.Candidates with expertise i... View Details Bookmark POOL Posting – Instructor, Counseling and Higher Education (Non-Tenure Track) 12/02/2025 11/30/2026 Counseling and Higher Education Athens, Ohio Instructors selected from this pool will teach courses within the Department of Counseling and Higher Education. Courses may include foundations of counseling, group counseling, ethics, assessment, multicultural counseling, career counseling, practicum or internship supervision, and other program-specific offerings depending on departmental needs. Courses may be online, in-person, or hybrid. View Details Bookmark Pool Posting - Instructor, Counseling and Higher Education (non-tenure track) 03/16/2026 03/02/2027 Counseling and Higher Education Athens, Ohio Instructors selected from this pool will teach fully online courses in the Applied Human Services program. Courses focus on foundational knowledge and skills relevant to careers in human services and community support roles. View Details Bookmark Educational Research and Evaluation Instructor POOL POSTING 08/07/2026 08/09/2027 Educational Studies Athens, Ohio The Department of Educational Studies in Ohio University’s Patton College of Education invites nominations and applications for an adjunct instructor pool within the department of Educational Studies. Applications should be sent to noted link above. Nominations may be sent to Educational Studies department chair, Dr. Jesse Strycker (strycker@ohio.edu). Nominees will then be requested to complet... View Details Bookmark Instructor, English (Part-time, Non-tenure track) POOL POSTING 06/03/2026 05/30/2027 English Athens, Ohio The English department is seeking applicants for a part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor position at the Athens campus for the Fall 2026 semester and the 2026-2027 academic year. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will review and select candidat... View Details Bookmark School of Nursing Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Eastern Campus, Beginning Fall Semester 2026 ( POOL POSTING) 04/06/2026 09/15/2026 ESTRN Nursing Eastern (St. Clairsville, Ohio) The Ohio University School of Nursing Eastern Campus seeks adjunct clinical focus faculty candidates with an emphasis on teaching clinical competencies with bachelor’s degree nursing students. These positions are term positions and will be filled as needs arise for the Eastern campus. Faculty are expected to plan, implement, and evaluate instruction for student clinical and simulation lab exper... View Details Bookmark School of Nursing Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Eastern Campus, Beginning Academic Year 2025-2026 (POOL POSTING) 04/24/2025 05/31/2026 ESTRN Nursing Eastern (St. Clairsville, Ohio) The Ohio University School of Nursing Eastern Campus seeks adjunct clinical focus faculty candidates with an emphasis on teaching clinical competencies with bachelor’s degree nursing students. These positions are term positions and will be filled as needs arise for the Eastern campus. Faculty are expected to plan, implement, and evaluate instruction for student clinical and simulation lab exper... View Details Bookmark Instructor (part-time) College of Business Finance Academic year 2026-2027 (POOL) 05/18/2026 04/14/2027 Finance, College of Business Athens, Ohio We are accepting resumes for potential openings in the College of Business Finance department for summer 2026 and the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting.Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill... View Details Bookmark Instructor, Geography (non-tenure track, part-time) POOL POSTING 07/16/2026 07/15/2027 Geography Athens, Ohio Applications for the positions will be considered to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions for the Department of Geography. The selected candidates may teach a large introduction level class or combined undergraduate and graduate courses. Duties include student assessment and may include teaching a lab. View Details Bookmark Instructor, Biomedical Sciences (part-time, non-tenure track, POOL POSTING) Campus of Choice 01/07/2026 01/07/2027 HCOM - Biomedical Sciences Athens, Ohio, Dublin, Ohio, Cleveland, Ohio Instructors are needed to teach in the areas of human anatomy, physiology, histology and/or other general biomedical science related specialties in the Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine. Teaching workload can include but is not limited to classroom group learning activities (preparing teaching objectives, reading lists, learning assessments, creating pre-recorded tutorials and problem se... View Details Bookmark Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Tenure Track) Diabetes Mellitus and Cardiometabolic Disorders, Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine, Athens Campus (3 positions available) 07/30/2026 09/20/2026 HCOM - Diabetes Institute Athens, Ohio The Diabetes Institute (DI) within the Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine (HCOM) at Ohio University is undergoing a targeted expansion to complement and strengthen its research portfolio. As part of this growth, DI/HCOM is seeking applications for three research-intensive, full-time (academic year) tenured or tenure-track faculty members at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Profes... View Details Bookmark Physician Instructor, Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine, part-time, non tenure-track, (Athens, Cleveland, or Dublin Ohio) (AY 26-27 Pool Posting) Periodic Engagement Role 07/01/2026 06/30/2027 HCOM - Executive Dean's Office Dublin, Ohio, Athens, Ohio, Cleveland, Ohio About the Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine:Mission:We pride ourselves on our strong focus on our mission: training osteopathic primary care physicians to serve Ohio.Our medical school educates physicians committed to practice in Ohio, emphasizes primary care, engages in focused research, and embraces both Appalachian and urban communities. Integral to this mission, our college community... View Details Bookmark Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine, Athens Campus (Pool Posting) 04/06/2026 04/05/2027 HCOM - Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) Athens, Ohio Position Description:The Ohio University Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine (OU-HCOM) is seeking an Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) physician for a part-time (16 hours per week) faculty teaching position at the Athens, Ohio campus.Applicants should possess a strong desire to teach and advise osteopathic medical students within the curriculum and contribute to the success of the He... View Details Bookmark Instructor, OMM, Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine (AY 26-27 Pool Posting) Periodic Engagement Role 07/30/2026 06/30/2027 HCOM - Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) Dublin, Ohio, Athens, Ohio, Cleveland, Ohio The Ohio University Heritage College of Osteopathic Medicine (OU-HCOM) is seeking Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) physicians for in-person, faculty teaching positions across the state of Ohio. Positions can include regular but low frequency teaching for medical students in their first two years of medical school on one of our three campuses in Athens, Cleveland, or Dublin, Ohio, and/or ... View Details Bookmark Instructor, Pharmacy, Adjunct, Non Tenure Track, (POOL POSTING) 11/14/2025 06/30/2027 HCOM - Primary Care Athens, Ohio, Dublin, Ohio, Cleveland, Ohio Position Description:The Heritage College is seeking applications for adjunct Instructors of Pharmacy to participate in the delivery of our integrated medical curriculum on our Athens, Cleveland, or Dublin, Ohio Campuses on an as needed basis. Selected instructors will join a diverse group of faculty in the Department of Primary Care, allowing the opportunity to gain training and expertise in a... View Details Bookmark Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor, Endocrinology or Diabetology, (Non Tenure Track) Part-Time, Athens Campus 11/14/2025 06/30/2027 HCOM - Specialty Medicine Athens, Ohio We are seeking an emerging or established clinical researcher with a focus on diabetes. This applicant will join a group of active, extramurally funded investigators within the Ohio University Diabetes Institute. This role is ideal for a physician interested in joining a team to gain experience in clinical research to contribute to the success of research programs that focus on the following to... View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 Next Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
