    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57591": {
      "title": "Ohio University - Job Site | Assistant Professor of Instruction, Nursing",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Assistant Professor of Instruction, Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Assistant Professor of Instruction, Nursing Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application and attach all required documents which include: Cover Letter CV/Resume List of 3 professional references with current contact information including email addresses Teaching philosophy statement, Unofficial transcripts Current RN license (attached under the “Other” document type) Failure to submit and properly upload all required documents, including your RN license, will result in your application being auto disqualified. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Instruction, Nursing Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the online application and attach all required documents which include: Cover Letter CV/Resume List of 3 professional references with current contact information including email addresses Teaching philosophy statement, Unofficial transcripts Current RN license (attached under the “Other” document type) Failure to submit and properly upload all required documents, including your RN license, will result in your application being auto disqualified. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, and retirement. Posting Number 20163228F Job Description Ohio University School of Nursing is seeking two non-tenure track faculty candidates for traditional on-campus BSN students. These are full-time, 9-month positions at the Assistant Professor of Instruction rank at the Athens campus. The candidates will be responsible to plan, implement, and be responsible for BSN student instruction. Didactic instruction will be assigned based on expertise and credentials. Assigned didactic teaching modalities will be face-to-face. In addition, online class delivery may be assigned as needed, based on expertise and credentials. Successful candidates may be expected to provide clinical site, laboratory, and didactic instruction to BSN student learners for all BSN courses. Additional expectations include (but are not limited to): Meeting with course faculty to develop course expectations. Identifying students’ needs in terms of objectives of the relevant course. Providing instruction to students at the clinical sites, laboratory/simulation settings, and classroom to acquire professional attitudes, knowledge, and skills. Assisting students in using problem-solving techniques. Successful candidates will be required to be on campus throughout the academic year (August through May). Teaching assignments/instructional responsibilities will be based on candidate expertise and/or credentials. All School of Nursing faculty members are expected to collaboratively and actively engage in the planning, implementation, and evaluation of student instruction and to participate in School of Nursing governance to ensure program standards and outcomes are fully met. Minimum Qualifications A minimum of a Master of Science in Nursing ( MSN ) degree from an accredited school of professional nursing is required. An active and unencumbered Ohio Registered Nurse (RN) license, or eligibility for obtaining and maintaining an Ohio RN license is required. Must have Ohio RN license prior to start date. An ability to obtain and maintain an RN license in states other than Ohio where BSN student clinical experiences occur will be required (e.g., West Virginia). Licensed as an RN in the United States for a minimum of two years is required. A minimum of two years (24 months full-time equivalent) of work experience as an RN in the United States is required. Preferred Qualifications Three plus years of teaching clinical, lab and didactic to RN students is preferred. Prior experience with student clinical coordination is preferred. Department Nursing-Athens Pay Rate The salary for this position is $68,500. Ohio University also offers employees a generous benefits package which includes health benefits and education benefits for employees and eligible dependents. Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. User Selection Field Job Open Date 09/01/2026 Posting Close Date Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, please apply by 10/1/2026. Employment Type full-time term Job Category Instructional and Clinical Faculty Months 9 month Planning Unit College of Health Sciences & Professions Work Schedule To be determined based on workload assignment. Typically, Monday through Friday with occasional weekend(s). Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Cora Arledge, arledgec@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio University is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Unofficial transcripts Other (See Special Instructions to Applicants for Details) Teaching philosophy statement Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold at least a Master’s Degree in Nursing (MSN)? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two years (24 months full time equivalent) of work experience as an RN in the United States? Yes No * Do you hold a current active and unencumbered Ohio RN license or are you eligible to obtain an unencumbered Ohio RN licensure prior to hire? Yes No * I have included a copy of my RN license with this application. (Failure to do so will result in an auto-disqualification.) Yes No * Do you have the ability to obtain and maintain an RN license in states other than Ohio where BSN student clinical experience occurs may also be required (e.g., West Virginia)? Yes No * Do you hold a current active and unencumbered Ohio RN license or multi-state license? Yes No Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
